{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check && git status --short; tail -10 formal/last_run-wwFTYtCom.log; cat implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n?? implementation_notes.md\nSBY 23:11:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:05:05  waiting for solver (5 minutes)\nSBY 23:16:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:10:05  waiting for solver (10 minutes)\nSBY 23:20:16 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:13:27  Status: passed\nSBY 23:20:17 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\nSBY 23:20:17 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\nSBY 23:20:17 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:13:32 (812)\nSBY 23:20:17 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:05:39 (339)\nSBY 23:20:17 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\nSBY 23:20:17 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\nSBY 23:20:17 [reg_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\n# Specialize divider updates by divisor magnitude\n\n`alu.sv` classifies the unsigned divisor magnitude at the prefix update. Below `2^16`, it processes a six-bit prefix and six updates of two radix-4 steps with 19-bit trials. For a zero divisor, those steps produce all-one quotient digits and shift the upper remainder bits directly. At `2^16` and above, it processes an 18-bit prefix and six full-width radix-4 updates. The prefix resolves one digit with 21-bit trials below `2^18`. At that threshold and above, the prefix quotient is zero. Both modes reuse the full-width final step and hold the result in phase 1 until consume.\n\nIn the split ALU instance, division uses the forwarded M-extension operand inputs. The standalone ALU uses `a` and `b`. The ALTOPS divider uses the same operand routing and retains the seven-update schedule. The ALU tests exercise signed and unsigned quotient and remainder near both magnitude thresholds, the boundaries of the 18-bit prefix digit, and held results in both modes.\n\nThe first timing run found the six-bit prefix on the worst setup path in the median placements. The revised register input decodes the update enables in parallel with the trials and gates each source with its one-hot enable. The large prefix computes the `3D` trial as `shifted + D - 4D`, using carry-save logic and one carry-propagating addition.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint and all five cocotb suites passed, including 29 ALU cases. `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed for all five ELFs after `make bench` built the random traces. Trace tests ran with both zero-wait and stalled buses.\n- The candidate and champion both completed stalled CoreMark in 3,202,739 marker-bracketed cycles for 10 iterations. The candidate UART printed `Correct operation validated.` and the canonical CRCs `e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a`, and `fcaf`.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retirement ALTOPS checks with zero failures or retries. The register consistency check took 13 minutes and 32 seconds. The preprocessed ALTOPS RTL matches the source staged for that run.\n\n## Gowin placement\n\n| Build | Option 0 MHz | Option 1 MHz | Option 2 MHz | Median MHz | CoreMark iter/s |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Champion `hyp-20261119-003-r10s2` | 76.343 | 86.757 | 86.757 | 86.757 | 270.88 |\n| Magnitude split | 74.153 | 77.313 | 77.313 | 77.313 | 241.40 |\n\nThe local champion build reproduced the logged frequencies. `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` reproduced the candidate results and reported 4,390 logic cells and 996 registers. The split moved the limiting path to instruction replay in all three placements. In options 1 and 2, the critical path runs from the replay validity bitmap to the replay entry RAM. The candidate median is below the scratch implementation's 83.243 MHz and the 90.75 MHz promotion threshold, giving a 10.89% fitness regression from the champion.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
