{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_46", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short --untracked-files=all && git diff --stat && sed -n '1,180p' implementation_notes.md\"", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? implementation_notes.md\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv           | 31 ++++++++----------\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv       |  2 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv       | 46 +++++++++++----------------\n cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv    | 62 +++++++-----------------------------\n cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv       | 16 ++++++----\n cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv       | 38 +++++++---------------\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | 67 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---\n 7 files changed, 129 insertions(+), 133 deletions(-)\n# Squash decode through the ID/EX valid bit\n\n## Implementation\n\n- IF passes the raw instruction and `io_imemReady` to ID. Data backpressure and divider wait hold both ID/EX payload and validity. On advance, ID/EX captures the payload and sets validity to `imem_ready && !load_use && !redirect`. Reset clears the valid bit.\n- Load-use detection requires a valid EX load and a ready fetch and compares both raw source register fields against the nonzero load destination. Redirect goes directly from EX to the PC and ID/EX valid bit. A redirect takes priority over a PC hold.\n- EX requires a valid instruction for redirect and divider launch. On EX/MEM advance, memory controls and post-trap register write are qualified by `id_ex.valid && !div_wait`. The retained MEM/WB register-write control keeps its result eligible for bypass across a data stall after its retirement valid clears.\n- The final implementation also shares the resolved EX target between the PC, alignment check, and RVFI next-PC. Branches and JAL use the PC-relative sum, and JALR uses the forwarded base plus immediate with bit 0 cleared. IF expresses redirect and sequential advance as a single PC update enable. This version measured a 49.128 MHz median after the initial valid-bit implementation measured 49.003 MHz.\n- Directed cocotb cases drive valid store, jump, and load words on unready fetches and place each on a taken branch's discarded path. A discarded divide also checks that invalid EX slots cannot delay target issue. The tests check redirect priority across both bus holds, the first target retirement and its operands, contiguous RVFI order, all data-bus requests, and exactly one acceptance of the stalled older store.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall` and no warnings.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 checks on the final RTL in a scratch checkout layout under `$TMPDIR`. It auto-selected the single-retirement wrapper and ALTOPS checks. Zero formal failures and zero formal fix attempts.\n- All five pytest runners for the bench cocotb suite passed, including the new pipeline cases.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed selftest with and without stalls and the stalled CoreMark CRC checks. The Makefile's local build needs `NRET=1` explicitly because the cosim build script defaults to two channels.\n\n## Gowin timing and CoreMark\n\n`make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1` measured **109.38 iterations/s** from 10 iterations over **4,491,485 marker-bracketed cycles**. The placement options measured 47.515, 49.128, and 49.128 MHz, with **49.128 MHz** median. The cycle count matched the champion. Fitness rose **4.61%** from 104.56 iterations/s, clearing the 4.6% margin by about **0.005 MHz**. Option 0 used 2,769 logic cells and 563 registers.\n\nThe redirect and load-use signals feed ID/EX validity only. The payload's capture enable depends on data backpressure and divider wait. The former EX-to-IF-to-hazard path into the ID/EX payload is absent from the worst setup paths. The median options are limited by the five-step divider update from `partial_q_31_s1` to `partial_q_44_s0`, with a 25.649 ns arrival time. Regfile-to-data-memory paths follow closely. The small margin makes the measured gain sensitive to placement.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
