{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_166","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'diff -qr cores/bench/rtl \"$TMPDIR/bench-compare.8pK93Bbv/cores/bench/rtl\" && diff -qr cores/bench/test \"$TMPDIR/bench-compare.8pK93Bbv/cores/bench/test\" -x '\"'*.xml' -x '__pycache__' && sed -n '1,140p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Shared execute comparator\n\nEX compares forwarded rs1 against the existing ALU B operand. It computes\nequality and unsigned less-than once. For a signed comparison with differing\nsign bits, the sign of rs1 supplies the result. Branch funct3 selects equality\nor less-than and its low bit inverts the predicate for BNE, BGE, and BGEU.\nDecoder validation and the existing target alignment check qualify branch\nredirects.\n\nEX selects the signedness for the current instruction and passes a single\nless-than bit to the ALU. The core uses that bit for both set-less-than\noperations, and the standalone ALU defaults to its local comparisons. The\ncomparison is combinational and uses the existing forwarding and retirement\nschedule.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed. All 105 cocotb tests passed, including both outcomes\n  for all six branch predicates, reserved and misaligned branches, equal\n  operands, opposite signs, SLTIU sign extension, and adjacent load forwarding\n  to BLT, SLT, and SLTU under instruction and data backpressure.\n- `formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retirement checks on the first run\n  of the selected RTL, with zero failures.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` passed the self-test and all three random reference\n  traces with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark matched seedcrc 0xe9f5,\n  crclist 0xe714, crcmatrix 0x1fd7, crcstate 0x8e3a, and crcfinal 0xfcaf.\n  The start-to-stop interval was 3,987,921 cycles for both this RTL and the\n  champion.\n\n## Gowin result\n\nPlacement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 60.501, 61.529, and 61.529 MHz, with\n3,180 logic cells versus 3,211 for the champion. The median gives 154.29\nCoreMark iterations per second, about 0.71% below the champion. It falls short\nof the 64.823 MHz acceptance threshold. The option-0 limiting path runs from\nregister-file readback to the branch predictor counter. The other placements\nare limited by data-memory readback into the EX/MEM ALU result.\n\nA byte-grouped comparator reached 61.637 MHz median with 3,241 logic cells.\nThe selected full-width expression uses less logic and keeps the comparator\nand its operand routing simpler.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
