{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_91","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'MPLCONFIGDIR=\"$TMPDIR/bench-mpl\" python3 -c '\"'from tools.orchestrator import allowed_patterns_for, offlimits_changes; paths = offlimits_changes(\\\".\\\", allowed_patterns_for(\\\"bench\\\")); print(paths); raise SystemExit(bool(paths))' && cat implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"[]\n# EX/MEM result and BTB retiming\n\n- EX/MEM captures the shift result and selector alongside the ordinary ALU result and holds them together through dmem backpressure. EX forwarding selects the registered shift or ordinary result under the existing writer and dependency checks. Load and multiply keep their direct bypass lanes. MEM/WB selects among the four result lanes with one-hot masks.\n- The standalone ALU still returns shifts on its ordinary output. SRL and SRA share a right shifter with a selectable fill bit. The shifter uses the forwarded operand and the low five bits of the selected register or immediate operand.\n- EX registers source eligibility, target range, the taken-alignment fault, branch hit, jump status, and both saturated counter candidates. IF and ID receive the pending update in the recovery cycle using the registered recovery target. The registered aligned-taken bit also selects the counter candidate because a taken alignment fault suppresses training. Source eligibility requires a live, advancing, legal instruction with an in-range, word-aligned PC. Reset clears eligibility.\n- The directed pipeline test runs with a ready load and with four stalled load cycles. It checks younger-load priority over an older write to the same register, SRA with a register amount of 63, all three immediate shifts, consecutive RVFI retirements, and the accepted dependent store.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint passed in hardware and ALTOPS modes. The single-retire ALTOPS formal gate passed all 53 checks with zero failures and no corrective retries.\n- All five cocotb suites passed, including same-PC counter bypass, same-index tag replacement, branch and JALR recovery, and both load-to-shift cases. RVFI cosimulation passed for selftest and all three random programs with and without bus stalls.\n- CoreMark passed the canonical CRCs in 3,987,921 marker-bracketed cycles with both stall streams enabled. The measured fitness was 179.27 iterations/s, up 5.97% from the champion.\n- Gowin placed at 70.499, 71.490, and 71.490 MHz with 3,349 logic cells and 847 registers. The 71.490 MHz median clears the 70.56 MHz acceptance floor and is 0.522 MHz below the scratch prototype. The median setup path runs from data RAM through load formatting and EX forwarding to the multiply-result register.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_92","type":"agent_message","text":"EX/MEM retiming passed Verilator lint, all 53 formal checks, all five cocotb suites, and RVFI cosimulation.\n\nGowin measured **71.490 MHz median**, 0.930 MHz above the acceptance floor and 0.522 MHz below the prototype. CoreMark reproduced **3,987,921 cycles** with canonical CRCs and scored **179.27 iterations/s**.\n\nThe implementation shares the SRL/SRA right shifter and reuses the registered aligned-taken bit for BTB counter selection. [Implementation notes](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261119-001-r6s0/implementation_notes.md)"}}
