{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check\ngit status --short --untracked-files=all\nsed -n '1,22p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# AUIPC in ID\n\nID captures the 20-bit sum of the fetch PC and U-immediate upper bits on the existing ID/EX payload write. The sum shares the PC's hold and validity handling. EX appends the saved low 12 PC bits and registers the result on the other-result lane. That lane selects jump links first, then AUIPC, then the ordinary ALU result. AUIPC is excluded from the add/subtract selector. The ALU receives forwarded `rs1` directly, and the existing EX/MEM bypass supplies AUIPC to the next instruction.\n\nThe RTL follows the proposed datapath. The pipeline regression exercises a wrong-path AUIPC, a stalled load ahead of the real AUIPC, and simultaneous fetch backpressure. AUIPC at `0x1020` with immediate `0xfffff000` writes `0x20`. The immediately following ADDI retires one cycle later and writes `0x27`.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings. All five cocotb suites passed.\n- RVFI cosimulation passed for selftest and all three random programs with both buses ready and with both stall streams enabled.\n- CoreMark matched all canonical CRCs and printed `Correct operation validated.` It completed 10 iterations in 3,987,921 marker-bracketed cycles with both stall streams enabled.\n- Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 measured 75.559, 78.576, and 78.576 MHz. Option 0 used 3,387 logic cells and 907 registers. The median result is 197.03 CoreMark iterations/s, up 7.16% at the same cycle count. Options 1 and 2 were limited by data-RAM readback into the registered EX target match.\n- The single-retire ALTOPS gate passed all 53 checks on the first run using `formal/run_all.sh` in a scratch copy.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
