{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'MULT36|MULT18|product_65_s1|mul_result_Z_5_s' cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p1/impl/gwsynthesis/core_bench.vg -m 12\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id') == 'hyp-20261119-001-r7s0': print(d.get('hypothesis'),d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{'motivation': 'The bench champion scores 183.88 CoreMark iterations per second at\\n73.329 MHz in 3,987,921 marker-bracketed cycles. In the median Gowin\\nplacements, the path from data RAM through load forwarding and the\\nAUIPC operand mux into the EX/MEM shifter register is within 0.001 ns\\nof the worst fetch-recovery path. Every instruction on the ordinary\\nALU operand A path passes through that mux. AUIPC can compute its\\nresult from the fetch PC and instruction bits before EX because its\\nimmediate has twelve zero low bits and uses no register operand.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"On the existing ID/EX payload capture edge, register the low 20 bits\\nof pc[31:12] + instr[31:12] alongside the PC. In EX, concatenate this\\nsum with the saved pc[11:0] to form the full modulo-2^32 AUIPC result.\\nDrive the ALU A input directly from forwarded rs1. Exclude AUIPC from\\nthe add/subtract result selector and put its value on the existing\\nother-result lane. Give jump links first priority on that lane,\\nAUIPC second, and the ordinary other ALU result third. Register the\\nlane and its existing one-hot control as usual so the immediately\\nfollowing instruction can use AUIPC via the normal EX/MEM bypass.\\nThe new upper sum uses the same hold and squash handling as the PC\\nand other ID/EX payload fields.\\n\\nAn isolated prototype measured 75.559, 78.576 and 78.576 MHz across\\nthe three Gowin placements using 3,387 logic cells and 907 registers\\nin option 0. The median placements are limited by data-RAM readback\\ninto the EX/MEM target match. CoreMark matched all canonical CRCs\\nin 3,987,921 marker-bracketed cycles with both bus stall streams,\\nyielding 197.03 iterations per second, up 7.16 percent. The prototype\\npassed all 53 single-retire ALTOPS checks, all five cocotb suites and\\nfull RVFI cosim on selftest and three random programs with and\\nwithout stalls. A directed case passed for AUIPC at PC 0x1020 with\\nimmediate 0xfffff000, modulo wrap to 0x20 and consecutive retirement\\nof the dependent ADDI while exercising both buses' backpressure.\\nReproduce the timing, cycle count and correctness checks on implementation.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 7, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Add a 20-bit auipc_upper field after direct_target in the ID/EX payload.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Capture the upper PC plus U-immediate sum on the existing ID/EX payload write.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Feed forwarded rs1 directly to the ALU and forward the early AUIPC sum on the other-result lane.'}]} \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
