{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_135","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short; sed -n '1,90p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Fetch replay and operand selection\n\n- IF starts one synchronous tagged replay read for the predicted successor and another for the resolved successor. The corrected address accounts for a ready bus response and last-word parking. The PC and one-hot replay source advance together. A ready bus word takes priority at issue.\n- Both 1,024-word replay arrays receive each accepted in-range fill while replay is armed and on the recovery that arms it. The validity bitmap and its same-bank bypass serve both read addresses. IF suppresses a read on a same-index collision and can retain the sampled fill for the held PC after checking its full address. Reset and FENCE.I clear the bank validity and held state.\n- The four candidate words independently address two asynchronous register-file reads each. The common source enables select both operands and the instruction at ID/EX. Each read applies write-first bypass from the shared WB port and returns zero for x0. Held instructions read the register file when issued.\n- EX/MEM captures the ordinary candidate and parked flag alongside the aligned JALR target. The recovery cycle compares the full addresses in byte groups. Direct jumps, branches, and fall-through keep early matches. ID continues to repair corrected BTB metadata, replay load consumers, and invalidate wrong-path work.\n- The two radix-4 divider updates and the bitmap RAM inference are retained. Parallel divider trials, grouped divider subtraction, distributed bitmap RAM, shared operand bypass selection, and a separate corrected-response enable for the ID payload were tried in intermediate builds. The retained implementation had the highest measured median.\n\n## Local validation\n\n- Verilator `--lint-only -Wall` passes.\n- The single-retirement `formal/run_all.sh` suite passed all 53 checks.\n- CoreMark cosim returns the canonical CRCs and `Correct operation validated.` with both stalls enabled. The markers occur at cycles 12,468 and 3,215,207, for 3,202,739 timed cycles. Selftest and all three committed random programs pass RVFI cosim with and without stalls.\n- All five cocotb runners pass, including 65 pipeline cases. The added cases cover a self-jump fill collision and ready-bus priority, both operand reads on ordinary and held replay with data backpressure, and write-first on the corrected JALR replay lane. The existing alias, FENCE.I, alignment, and parking cases pass.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 75.924, 77.047, and 77.047 MHz. The 77.047 MHz median yields 240.57 CoreMark iterations/s, below the 270.88 baseline and the promotion target. The divider recurrence is the worst setup path in all three placements. The corrected replay RAM through register-file selection into ID/EX is the next path in the median placements.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
