{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; git diff --stat; git diff --check; diff -qr cores/bench/rtl \\\"/srv/hwebench/tmp/7cb5c576/16ab9fad/bench-jalr.ZlPLb2/project/../final/cores/bench/rtl\\\"; sed -n '1,120p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n?? implementation_notes.md\n cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv      |  4 +++-\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------\n 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)\n# JALR prediction validation\n\n## Implementation\n\nEX validates the ordinary fetch candidate with four registered groups of independent carry checks. The checks require candidate bit 0 to be clear, anchor the carry into bit 1 from the two low operand bits, and check each transition through the carry into bit 31. Each transition compares the two carries after XORing both with the current immediate bit. This lets adjacent sign-extension bits cancel in the required carry expression.\n\nEX registers the direct target match and the JALR check enable with the parked-fetch qualification. It reduces the four JALR groups in the recovery cycle and combines that result with the direct target match. The fall-through match and EX advance pulse retain their existing register timing and hold behavior.\n\nThe ALU exposes the shared addition before the ADD/SUB result selection. EX masks its bit 0 to produce the full JALR target for alignment, BTB eligibility, recovery, and RVFI. The early tap removes the ADD/SUB selector from the target path.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\n- A combinational SAT proof established equality with ordinary candidate-PC comparison against masked 32-bit addition for arbitrary operands and candidates. It included direct targets and the parked-fetch qualifier.\n- The single-retirement formal gate, co-simulation, and three-option Gowin sweep for the final RTL are running in scratch copies.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
