{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"tail -6 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-850 && rg -n 'cleanup|ignore|lock|override' .gitignore tools/eval/_slots.py test/cosim/build.sh && sed -n '270,300p' tools/eval/fpga.py && git status --short --ignored\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Split RV32M arithmetic across existing register boundaries\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The 127.12 iter/s champion reaches 53.281 MHz median Gowin Fmax. Its\\nworst setup path runs through multiply and the ALU result select into\\nEX/MEM. The divider recurrence is close behind in both median placements.\\nA trace of the champion under both bus stalls counted 93,960 MULs and\\nno high-half multiplies, divides or remainders in 4,191,341 bracketed\\ncycles. Moving product reduction across EX/MEM can keep one multiply\\nper cycle for independent instructions. Shorter divider updates let\\nthe higher clock rate carry through to the full core.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The 127.12 iter/s champion reaches 53.281 MHz median Gowin Fmax. Its\\nworst setup path runs through multiply and the ALU r\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Split execute forwarding into ALU, multiply and load lanes\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current bench champion scores 127.12 CoreMark iterations per second at\\n53.281 MHz and 4,191,341 timed cycles. Its worst reported path ends at\\nthe EX/MEM ALU result register. The round-three structural trial removed\\nthe load-use bubble and reached 3,987,921 cycles. Prototyping that bypass\\non the current core put both the forwarding selects and memory readback\\non critical paths through the DSPs and the shared ALU result mux. The\\nforwarding network needs separate paths for results that become available\\nat different points in the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current bench champion scores 127.12 CoreMark iterations per second at\\n53.281 MHz and 4,191,341 timed cycles. Its \n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Derive queued fetch successors from the BTB request stream\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Replay of the existing 32-entry BTB estimated 57,035 wrong successors\\nover 4,191,341 CoreMark cycles. With one slot lost per redirect, better\\ndirection accuracy has limited upside. The prior four-entry\n…[4560 of 7632 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2a680ae213e27f4b]…\not in uart:\n        if 'Cannot validate operation' in uart:\n            return False, f'coremark_unvalidated_seed_or_size: {uart[-500:]}'\n        if 'ERROR' in uart or 'Errors detected' in uart:\n            return False, f'coremark_reported_error: {uart[-500:]}'\n        return False, f'coremark_validation_marker_missing: {uart[-500:]}'\n\n    checks = [\n        ('seedcrc',   _uart_int(uart, r'seedcrc\\s*:\\s*0x([0-9a-fA-F]+)', 16)),\n        ('crclist',   _uart_int(uart, r'\\[0\\]crclist\\s*:\\s*0x([0-9a-fA-F]+)', 16)),\n        ('crcmatrix', _uart_int(uart, r'\\[0\\]crcmatrix\\s*:\\s*0x([0-9a-fA-F]+)', 16)),\n        ('crcstate',  _uart_int(uart, r'\\[0\\]crcstate\\s*:\\s*0x([0-9a-fA-F]+)', 16)),\n        ('crcfinal',  _uart_int(uart, r'\\[0\\]crcfinal\\s*:\\s*0x([0-9a-fA-F]+)', 16)),\n    ]\n    for name, got in checks:\n        expected = COREMARK_EXPECTED[name]\n        if got != expected:\n            return False, f'coremark_{name}_mismatch: expected 0x{expected:04x}, got {got}'\n\n!! .agent.last\n!! .agent.log\n!! formal/riscv-formal\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
