{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.formal import _cleanup_formal_workdir\n\nworktree = Path.cwd()\nfor filename in (\\\"selftest.elf\\\", \\\"coremark.elf\\\", \\\"random1.elf\\\", \\\"random2.elf\\\", \\\"random3.elf\\\"):\n    (worktree / \\\"bench\\\" / \\\"programs\\\" / filename).unlink(missing_ok=True)\nfor work_id in (\\\"ReplayFinalR9s2\\\", \\\"wgyCvKPTb\\\"):\n    _cleanup_formal_workdir(worktree, \\\"bench\\\", work_id)\n    (worktree / \\\"formal\\\" / f\\\"last_run-{work_id}.log\\\").unlink(missing_ok=True)\n'\ngit diff --check && git status --short --untracked-files=all\nsed -n '1,110p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? implementation_notes.md\n# Bench replay RAM\n\n`if_stage.sv` uses a synchronous 4,096 × 39-bit replay RAM indexed by\nPC[13:2]. Each word packs validity, PC[19:14], and the instruction. The\nRAM reads from the same next-PC value that the ordinary fetch register\ncaptures. The next-PC mux uses one-hot selects for the predicted target,\nfall-through, and held PC. This improved the local median from 66.274 MHz\nwith the original mux to 68.560 MHz.\n\nReset and each advancing FENCE.I block replay immediately. The shared\nwrite port then clears validity at indices 0 through 4095, with the bus\ndriving the tag and instruction on every write. Invalidation restarts the\nsweep and clears the arm even when a taken prediction coincides with it.\nImem can supply instructions throughout the sweep. Taken predictions and\nrecoveries can arm replay during the sweep, and accepted ready imem words\nresume filling it after the final write. A sampled write strobe and\n12-bit index suppress the read/write collision, including the final\nscrub write. A ready bus response still supplies the accepted instruction\nand can refresh an existing replay word.\n\nThe pipeline tests warm the replay-specific fixtures and check bus\nretirement during a scrub, reset and consecutive FENCE.I restarts with\nimem backpressure, refill and replay after the scrub, stale-word\nsuppression at the last scrub index, tag mismatches on PC[19:14], and\nsimultaneous reads and fills at matching and distinct indices.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint completed without warnings. All five cocotb suites\n  passed, including the 50 pipeline cases.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 checks with the configured\n  single-retire wrapper and zero retries. The bounded formal checks\n  cover bus operation during startup. The directed pipeline tests\n  exercise replay at and after scrub completion.\n- Co-simulation matched selftest and all three random programs against\n  the reference with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark produced the\n  canonical CRCs and validated operation.\n- Gowin mapped replay to 10 BSRAMs. Option 0 used 3,448 logic cells,\n  926 registers, and 14 BSRAMs total. Placement options 0, 1, and 2\n  reached 66.153, 68.560, and 68.560 MHz, respectively. Option 0 was\n  limited by EX recovery to the replay read address. Options 1 and 2\n  were limited by data RAM to the EX shifter.\n- CoreMark took 3,183,041 marker-bracketed cycles across 10 iterations,\n  9,068 fewer cycles than the champion. The 68.560 MHz median yields\n  215.39 iterations/s and is 8.910 MHz below the 77.47 MHz promotion\n  threshold.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
