r.sv + checks.cfg).\n    \"\"\"\n    p = Path(core_yaml_path)\n    if not p.exists():\n        return 2\n    y = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()) or {}\n    n = y.get(\"nret\", 2)\n    if n not in (1, 2):\n        raise ValueError(f\"core.yaml nret must be 1 or 2, got {n!r}\")\n    return n\n\n# Floor on how many .sby tasks must pass for a \"formal: green\" result.\n# V0 baseline produces 53. Allow some slack (≥50) s\n…[31470 of 34542 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:df9d64da65f20004]…\nlftest with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark completed in 3,202,739 bracketed cycles with the canonical CRCs and `Correct operation validated.`\\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 checks with the standard single-channel wrapper and ALTOPS checks. No formal fix attempts were needed.\\n- The selected block-RAM design uses the original one-hot ordinary PC selector. The Gowin flow measured 78.949, 81.195, and 81.195 MHz across placement options 0, 1, and 2. The divider limited all three placements. The 81.195 MHz median is 6.4% below the 86.757 MHz champion at the same CoreMark cycle count.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T00:16:51.243693Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r14s2 (regression, -6.41%): Reading BTB tags and targets synchronously from block RAM alongside replay preserved stalled CoreMark cycles with correction-only allocation and same-index write forwarding, while the divider limited all three Gowin placements and median Fmax fell from 86.757 to 81.195 MHz.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
