{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_19", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git show HEAD -- cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv'", "aggregated_output": "commit bdc9d533182a9845aa1cb4ee63417e6a01a7b17c\nAuthor: HWE Bench <hwe-bench@localhost>\nDate:   Thu Nov 19 17:03:56 2026 +0100\n\n    hyp-20261119-002-r4s1: Split execute forwarding into ALU, multiply and load lanes (+22.2%)\n\ndiff --git a/cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv b/cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\nindex 622ee3c..c63e3a0 100644\n--- a/cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+++ b/cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\n@@ -1,38 +1,32 @@\n-// rtl/forward_unit.sv\n-//\n-// Operand forwarding. For each rs in the EX-stage's source list, picks\n-// where the freshest value lives:\n-//   00 (NONE)    : ID/EX register's rs?_val (= regfile read of one cycle ago)\n-//   01 (EX_MEM)  : the in-flight ALU result from the EX/MEM register\n-//   10 (MEM_WB)  : the WB-stage's regfile-write data\n-//\n-// Priority is EX/MEM > MEM/WB > none (younger writer wins, x0 always 0).\n-//\n-// Latency:        combinational.\n-// RVFI fields:    n/a — feeds rs1_rdata / rs2_rdata via EX-stage muxes.\n+// Qualify the matches captured by ID with the producers' writer controls.\n module forward_unit (\n-  input  logic [4:0] id_ex_rs1,\n-  input  logic [4:0] id_ex_rs2,\n-  input  logic [4:0] ex_mem_rd,\n+  input  logic [1:0] ex_match,\n+  input  logic [1:0] mem_match,\n   input  logic       ex_mem_w_en,\n-  input  logic [4:0] mem_wb_rd,\n+  input  logic       ex_mem_mul,\n+  input  logic       ex_mem_load,\n   input  logic       mem_wb_w_en,\n-  output logic [1:0] fwd_rs1,\n-  output logic [1:0] fwd_rs2\n+  output fwd_sel_t   fwd_rs1,\n+  output fwd_sel_t   fwd_rs2\n );\n \n-  // Yosys's Verilog frontend rejects SV-style `function … return …`,\n-  // so the per-rs selection is open-coded in two always_comb blocks.\n-  always_comb begin\n-    if      (ex_mem_w_en && ex_mem_rd != 5'b0 && ex_mem_rd == id_ex_rs1) fwd_rs1 = 2'd1;\n-    else if (mem_wb_w_en && mem_wb_rd != 5'b0 && mem_wb_rd == id_ex_rs1) fwd_rs1 = 2'd2;\n-    else                                                                  fwd_rs1 = 2'd0;\n-  end\n+  logic [1:0] younger, older;\n \n-  always_comb begin\n-    if      (ex_mem_w_en &&\n…[1770 of 4842 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:42030e0b08a65714]…\nif_id_rs2,         // IF/ID instr[24:20]  (next rs2)\n   input  logic       div_wait,          // EX is holding a divide/remainder\n   input  logic       imem_ready,\n   input  logic       dmem_ready,\n   input  logic       ex_mem_mem_op,\n-  output logic       fetch_ready,       // imem delivered without load-use\n+  output logic       fetch_ready,\n   output logic       hold_id,           // older instruction still in EX\n   output logic       stall_ex_mem,      // EX/MEM register holds\n   output logic       hold_mem_wb        // MEM/WB clears valid only;\n                                         // data fields stay (for fwd)\n );\n \n-  logic load_use_hazard;\n   logic dmem_stall;\n \n-  assign load_use_hazard = imem_ready && id_ex_load && id_ex_rd != 5'b0\n-                        && (id_ex_rd == if_id_rs1 || id_ex_rd == if_id_rs2);\n-  assign fetch_ready = imem_ready && !load_use_hazard;\n+  assign fetch_ready = imem_ready;\n \n   assign dmem_stall = !dmem_ready && ex_mem_mem_op;\n   assign hold_id = dmem_stall || div_wait;\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_20", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,150p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-002-r4s1.yaml && ls -la .tmp\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261119-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Split execute forwarding into ALU, multiply and load lanes\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current bench champion scores 127.12 CoreMark iterations per second at\n  53.281 MHz and 4,191,341 timed cycles. Its worst reported path ends at\n  the EX/MEM ALU result register. The round-three structural trial removed\n  the load-use bubble and reached 3,987,921 cycles. Prototyping that bypass\n  on the current core put both the forwarding selects and memory readback\n  on critical paths through the DSPs and the shared ALU result mux. The\n  forwarding network needs separate paths for results that become available\n  at different points in the pipeline.\nhypothesis: |\n  Register the ordinary ALU or jump-link result and the multiply result as\n  independent EX/MEM lanes. Run multiply from the raw forwarded operands\n  so the immediate and AUIPC selection is off its input path. Use one\n  signed 33-by-33 product, extending rs1 with its sign bit for MULH and\n  MULHSU and rs2 with its sign bit for MULH. Use a zero extension otherwise.\n  Select bits 31:0 for MUL and 63:32 for the upper-half variants before\n  registering the multiply lane. Route the existing ALTOPS multiply\n  formulas through the same lane on the same schedule. DIV and REM stay\n  in the ordinary lane with the current launch and completion schedule.\n  Keep the standalone ALU's default output behavior for the existing\n  arithmetic vectors and enable the split outputs in the core instance.\n\n  Add the formatted data-memory response as a parallel MEM-to-EX lane.\n  Use address and width to select response bytes in parallel and apply\n  sign extension directly from the selected byte or halfword sign bit.\n  In ID, compare both incoming source addresses against the destinations\n  in EX and MEM. Latch the two pairs of matches with the instruction so\n  the comparisons are complete when the producers reach EX/MEM and\n  MEM/WB. In EX, qualify those matches with the producer's actual writer\n  controls and use mutually exclusive selects for th\n…[3513 of 6585 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:db79504c8b2c5835]…\nmatches, producer qualifications and parallel result lanes. Preserve the nret=1 memory and RVFI interfaces.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Remove the decode load-use interlock and preserve instruction readiness, data backpressure and divider holds.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Require consecutive retirement for a ready load and its immediate ordinary or multiply consumer. Check load-to-divide latency, forwarding across a stalled load on both operands, an older writer behind a trapped load, branch recovery, and exactly-once memory side effects.\"\ntotal 216\ndrwxrwx--T+  5 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 19 17:03 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 15 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 19 17:04 ..\ndrwxrwx---+  2 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 19 17:01 agent-logs\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup   2225 Nov 19 15:04 env.json\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup 173146 Nov 19 17:04 orchestrator.log\ndrwxr-x---  11 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 19 15:04 riscv-formal-eval\ndrwxrwx---+  2 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 19 15:04 sandbox-probe\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
