esis\": \"Build two EX operand paths from the existing one-hot bypass lanes.\\nRoute formatted MEM load data only to the branch comparators,\\neffective-address adder and store-data path. Feed integer ALU,\\nmultiply, divider and a separate JALR target adder from the\\nregister-backed lanes. For a live instruction on that path whose\\nyoungest eligible producer is a load, hold ID/EX and fetch. On\\nthe edge when the older load is accepted, insert one EX/MEM bubble,\\nretain the forwarded value of each other operand in ID/EX and\\npromote the matching load dependencies to MEM/WB. The consumer\\nexecut\n…[73428 of 76500 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b5d89150ecd68b14]…\nced the candidate results and reported 4,390 logic cells and 996 registers. The split moved the limiting path to instruction replay in all three placements. In options 1 and 2, the critical path runs from the replay validity bitmap to the replay entry RAM. The candidate median is below the scratch implementation's 83.243 MHz and the 90.75 MHz promotion threshold, giving a 10.89% fitness regression from the champion.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-19T22:27:58.419730Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r12s0 (regression, -10.88%): Specializing radix-4 updates by divisor magnitude moved the median Gowin timing limit to the replay validity bitmap feeding entry RAM, where the slower post-route path dropped Fmax from 86.757 to 77.313 MHz and reduced CoreMark throughput at unchanged cycle count.\"}\nls: cannot access '/srv/hwebench/tmp/7cb5c576/161481a0': No such file or directory\nls: cannot access '/srv/hwebench/tmp/7cb5c576/161481a0/bench-structural.ZB8tfqmA': No such file or directory\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
