herwise.\\nSelect bits 31:0 for MUL and 63:32 for the upper-half variants before\\nregistering the multiply lane. Route the existing ALTOPS multiply\\nformulas through the same lane on the same schedule. DIV and REM stay\\nin the ordinary lane with the current launch and completion schedule.\\nKeep the standalone ALU's default output behavior for the existing\n…[16610 of 19682 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0c8a292b2dec7370]…\nions 0, 1, and 2 reached 60.501, 61.529, and 61.529 MHz, with\\n3,180 logic cells versus 3,211 for the champion. The median gives 154.29\\nCoreMark iterations per second, about 0.71% below the champion. It falls short\\nof the 64.823 MHz acceptance threshold. The option-0 limiting path runs from\\nregister-file readback to the branch predictor counter. The other placements\\nare limited by data-memory readback into the EX/MEM ALU result.\\n\\nA byte-grouped comparator reached 61.637 MHz median with 3,241 logic cells.\\nThe selected full-width expression uses less logic and keeps the comparator\\nand its operand routing simpler.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-19T16:53:04.192463Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r5s0 (regression, -0.71%): Sharing the EX comparator on forwarded operands for branches and SLT/SLTU saved 31 Gowin logic cells, while data-memory readback into the EX/MEM ALU result still limited median Fmax to 61.529 MHz and reduced CoreMark throughput at the same cycle count.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
