load clear. The same squash can be expresse\n{'id': 'hyp-20261119-001-r3s0', 'hypothesis': {'motivation': 'The 114.06 iter/s bench champion has a 47.807 MHz median Gowin Fmax.\\nIts reported 26.403 ns, 154-cell worst path starts and ends at divider\\npartial registers and crosses five dependent restoring subtract/select\\nsteps. The previous validity-only squash experiment exposed the same\\ndivider path. Shortening the recurrence exposed the next timing limit\\nin Gowin, from the register file through the multiplier and ALU result\\nmux to the \n{'id': 'hyp-20261119-001-r4s0', 'hypothesis': \n…[2938 of 6010 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6d5a320fb43ce867]…\nd tree. Both the wide\n{'id': 'hyp-20261119-001-r10s0', 'hypothesis': {'motivation': 'The current champion runs CoreMark in 3,202,739 cycles at a median\\n80.427 MHz. Both median Gowin placements trace the limiting path from\\nnormal_pc_q[11] through the same-bank validity bypass, slot lookup,\\nfetch acceptance and successor muxes to the synchronous replay address.\\nThe bank match currently selects all 32 bits before the slot lookup,\\nand ordinary acceptance controls multiple successive PC muxes.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Comp\n{'id': 'hyp-20261119-003-r10s2', 'hypothesis': {'motivation': 'The champion runs 10 CoreMark iterations in 3,202,739 cycles at a median\\n80.427 MHz. Both median placements are limited by the IF path into the\\nreplay validity RAM. IF currently forms two full-width ordinary successors\\nfor the pending BTB training outcomes and then selects between them and the\\ncorrected successors. A profile counted about 59,000 control-flow\\ncorrections through the end marker. Doubling the BTB saved only 0.22%\\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
