{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261119-003-r10s2|hyp-20261119-00[12]-r10s[01]|hyp-20261119-002-r9s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n r=json.loads(l); print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"],r.get(\\\"fitness\\\"),r.get(\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"),r.get(\\\"cycles\\\"),r.get(\\\"critical_path\\\"),r.get(\\\"logic_levels\\\")); print(r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\"))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261119-003-r10s2|hyp-20261119-00[12]-r10s[01]|hyp-20261119-002-r9s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n r=json.loads(l); print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"],r.get(\\\"fitness\\\"),r.get(\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"),r.get(\\\"cycles\\\"),r.get(\\\"critical_path\\\"),r.get(\\\"logic_levels\\\")); print(r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\"))'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-002-r9s1 Split live load consumers at the execute boundary 251.12 80.427 3202739 {'from': 'cpu/u_if/normal_pc_q_11_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/replay_valid_slots_replay_valid_slots_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -7.326, 'arrival_ns': 17.62, 'logic_cells': 16, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if']} 13\n# Split live load consumers at the execute boundary\n\nID predecodes the architectural source operands and retains both raw register fields for RVFI. EX keeps most consumers on register-backed forwarding, with a ready LW supplying the raw base for a dependent load and formatted load data supplying BEQ and BNE. The equality lane registers four byte predicates. Recovery reduces them and selects between the BTB counter candidates computed in EX. The single RVFI channel still retires at MEM/WB.\n\nWhen another consumer needs the live load, the load's accepting edge inserts one EX/MEM bubble. ID/EX retains the consumer, saves its other forwarded operands, and moves the load matches to MEM/WB. Older data-memory backpressure holds the request and its forwarding state. Divider launch, memory side effects, and BTB training are qualified by the corresponding instruction's advance.\n\nOrdinary fetch acceptance uses the unsquashed ID/EX candidate. The ordinary-PC BTB lookup computes both pending-training successors before the registered branch predicates select one. A corrected request can accept on the recovery beat using imem readiness and the older memory hold. On that beat it advances sequentially, and its metadata lookup uses the captured PC and the committed older BTB update. When the correction cannot accept on the recovery beat, its PC becomes the ordinary request for retry.\n\nReplay validity now uses 32 resettable bank flags and RAM-backed bitmaps to shorten lookup and update paths. The fetch bitmap read, replay word read, and PC register use the same selected next PC. A registered write bypass covers both bitmap read ports on a same-bank collision. FENCE.I clears all bank flags in one edge. The first subsequent fill in a bank repl\n…[7737 of 10809 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e50be56fdf61ff1e]…\n\n\nThe two median placements are limited by the registered dependency match through the EX target comparison. Bitmap-to-replay address, divider recurrence, and replay-to-register-file paths are nearly tied. Option 0 came in 10.414 MHz below the median. Gowin reports 4,393 logic cells, up 126 from the champion, and 994 registers.\n\n## Correctness checks\n\n- Verilator lint and all five cocotb suites passed. RVFI co-simulation passed for selftest and three random programs in both zero-wait and randomized bus-stall modes. CoreMark passed UART validation with both stalls enabled.\n- Combinational SAT proved baseline equivalence for the full-width successor, IF/ID bundle, prediction and parking decisions, replay hit and fill, and BTB update. A separate SAT check proved exactly one enabled source outside reset and zero enabled sources during reset.\n- Local ALTOPS passed all 53 checks through `formal/run_all.sh`. Register consistency (`reg_ch0`) passed in 11 minutes 14 seconds. The retained RTL passed on its first run.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
