{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_23", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg --no-line-number -i 'divider.*radix|radix.*divider|divider recurrence' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import sys,json\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n r=json.loads(l)\n print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"],r[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"])\n if r[\\\"id\\\"] in [\\\"hyp-20261119-002-r4s1\\\",\\\"hyp-20261119-001-r3s0\\\"]: print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"],r[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"])'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-001-r1s0 Use a shared six-round divider in execute 42.123\nhyp-20261119-001-r3s0 Shorten EX arithmetic paths to the divider and data memory 53.281\nShorten both paths within the current EX and MEM stages. Capture the\nfull unmasked JALR base-plus-immediate sum in a separate 32-bit\nEX/MEM field for load/store effective addresses. Use that field for\nthe data-memory address, byte lanes, alignment checks, load extraction\nand RVFI memory address. Hold it with the rest of EX/MEM under data\nbackpressure. Use bit-zero clearing only for JALR, and keep the ALU\nresult on the existing forwarding and register-write path. This lets\nGowin time memory addressing separately from multiply and divide.\n\nKeep the first update at two quotient bits. Replace the next six\nfive-bit updates with two radix-4 steps followed by one radix-2 step.\nFor a radix-4 step, concatenate the 32-bit unsigned partial remainder\nwith the next two dividend bits. In parallel, subtract D, 2D and 3D\nusing 35-bit zero-extended trials and choose the largest digit whose\ntrial has no borrow. Use the ordered borrow flags to form one-hot\nremainder selects for digits 0 through 3, so the remainder feeds the\nnext step through a single selection. Append the chosen quotient bits\nto the existing dividend/quotient shift state. This reduces the main\nrecurrence from five serial subtract/select stages to three.\n\nRegister 3D during the first update, in parallel with processing the\nleading two dividend bits. That first trial input is at most three\nbecause the initial remainder is zero. For a divisor above three the\nleading digit is zero. For divisors zero through three, determine the\nleading digit and remainder from the two dividend bits and the low\ndivisor bits directly. Use full-width divisor multiples in all later\nrounds. For D=0 the trials always select the maximum digit, giving an\nall-ones quotient and preserving the dividend magnitude as remainder.\nRetain the existing signed magnitude and result correction, including\nzero divisors and INT_MIN divided by -1.\n\nKeep\n…[8800 of 11872 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ccf01904471ec5dc]…\nt and all three random programs with no stalls and with both stall streams enabled.\n- CoreMark validated all canonical CRCs in 3,987,921 marker-bracketed cycles for 10 iterations with both stall streams enabled.\n\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax (MHz) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 62.201 |\n| 1 | 61.972 |\n| 2 | 61.972 |\n| Median | 61.972 |\n\nOption 0 used 3,211 logic cells, 719 registers, and two DSP resources. The worst option 0 path runs from data-memory readback to fetch-PC recovery. The median clock and bracketed cycles yield 155.40 CoreMark iterations per second, 22.25% above the 127.12 iter/s champion.\n\nhyp-20261119-003-r4s2 Derive queued fetch successors from the BTB request stream 56.469\nhyp-20261119-002-r7s1 Route immediate load forwarding through branch and address lanes 79.065\nhyp-20261119-002-r9s1 Split live load consumers at the execute boundary 80.427\nhyp-20261119-001-r10s0 Select fetch successors with one-hot enables 83.372\nhyp-20261119-003-r10s2 Select the BTB and recovery successors in parallel 86.757\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_24", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > /srv/hwebench/tmp/7cb5c576/6b2b6527/bench_experiment.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nimport sys\n\nroot = Path(__file__).parent / sys.argv[1]\nrtl = root / \\\"cores/bench/rtl\\\"\nrtl.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nshutil.copytree(\\\"cores/bench/rtl\\\", rtl)\nshutil.copy2(\\\"cores/bench/core.yaml\\\", rtl.parent)\nshutil.copytree(\\\"fpga\\\", root / \\\"fpga\\\")\nalu_path = rtl / \\\"alu.sv\\\"\nalu = alu_path.read_text()\nif sys.argv[1].startswith(\\\"div-radix16\\\"):\n    # k*D <= 15*(2**32-1), and all trials have a signed 37-bit difference.\n    decls = [\n        \\\"  logic [35:0] odd_multiple_q [1:7];\\\",\n        \\\"  logic [63:0] after_radix16;\\\",\n        \\\"  logic [36:0] shifted_four;\\\",\n        \\\"  logic [15:0] valid_digit, selected_digit;\\\",\n        \\\"  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\\\",\n        \\\"  logic [36:0] trials [1:15];\\\",\n        \\\"  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\\\",\n        \\\"  logic [31:0] radix16_r [0:15];\\\",\n        \\\"  logic [3:0] radix16_digit;\\\",\n        \\\"  logic [31:0] radix16_remainder;\\\",\n        \\\"\\\",\n        \\\"  assign shifted_four = {1'b0, partial_q[63:28]};\\\",\n        \\\"  assign radix16_r[0] = shifted_four[31:0];\\\",\n        \\\"  assign valid_digit[0] = 1'b1;\\\",\n    ]\n    for digit in range(1, 16):\n        odd = digit\n        shift = 0\n        while odd % 2 == 0:\n            odd //= 2\n            shift += 1\n        if odd == 1:\n            multiple = \\\"{5'b0, divisor_q}\\\"\n        elif odd == 3:\n            multiple = \\\"{3'b0, triple_divisor_q}\\\"\n        else:\n            multiple = f\\\"{{1'b0, odd_multiple_q[{odd//2}]}}\\\"\n        decls.append(f\\\"  assign trials[{digit}] = shifted_four - ({multiple} << {shift});\\\")\n        decls.append(f\\\"  assign valid_digit[{digit}] = \"'!trials[{digit}][36];\")\n        decls.append(f\"  assign radix16_r[{digit}] = trials[{digit}][31:0];\")\n    decls += [\n        \"  assign selected_digit = valid_digit & ~{1'\"'b0, valid_digit[15:1]};\\\",\n        \\\"  for (genvar n = 0; n < 4; ++n) begin : select_digit_bit\\\",\n        \\\"    logic [15:0] choices;\\\",\n        \\\"    for (genvar d = 0; d < 16; ++d) begin : digit_choice\\\",\n        \\\"      assign choices[d] = selected_digit[d] && 1'((d >> n) & 1);\\\",\n        \\\"    end\\\",\n        \\\"    assign radix16_digit[n] = |choices;\\\",\n        \\\"  end\\\",\n        \\\"  for (genvar n = 0; n < 32; ++n) begin : choose_remainder_bit\\\",\n        \\\"    logic [15:0] choices;\\\",\n        \\\"    for (genvar d = 0; d < 16; ++d) begin : remainder_choice\\\",\n        \\\"      assign choices[d] = selected_digit[d] & radix16_r[d][n];\\\",\n        \\\"    end\\\",\n        \\\"    assign radix16_remainder[n] = |choices;\\\",\n        \\\"  end\\\",\n        \\\"  assign after_radix16 = {radix16_remainder, partial_q[27:0], radix16_digit};\\\",\n        \\\"\\\",\n    ]\n    source = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(decls)\n    source = source.replace(\\\"odd_multiple_q [1:7]\\\", \\\"odd_multiple_q [2:7]\\\")\n    alu = alu.replace(\\\"  assign after_radix4_b = radix4_step(after_radix4_a, divisor_q, triple_divisor_q);\\\", source)\n    alu = alu.replace(\\\"after_radix4_a, after_radix4_b\\\", \\\"after_radix4_a\\\")\n    alu = alu.replace(\\\"      partial_q <= after_radix4_b;\\\", \\\"      partial_q <= after_radix16;\\\")\n    arith = {5:\\\"(x << 2) + x\\\", 7:\\\"(x << 3) - x\\\", 9:\\\"(x << 3) + x\\\", 11:\\\"(x << 3) + (x << 1) + x\\\", 13:\\\"(x << 4) - ((x << 1) + x)\\\", 15:\\\"(x << 4) - x\\\"}\n    alu = alu.replace(\\\"  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\\\\n    if (div_launch) begin\\\\n      partial_q\\\", \\\"  logic [35:0] x;\\\\n  assign x = {4'b0, divisor_q};\\\\n\\\\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\\\\n    if (div_launch) begin\\\\n      partial_q\\\")\n    append = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(f\\\"      odd_multiple_q[{d//2}] <= {expr};\\\" for d, expr in arith.items())\n    anchor = \\\"      triple_divisor_q <= {2'b0, divisor_q} + {1'b0, divisor_q, 1'b0};\\\"\n    alu = alu.replace(anchor, anchor + \\\"\\\\n\\\" + append)\nelif sys.argv[1].startswith(\\\"div-seg\\\"):\n    length = int(sys.argv[1].rsplit(\\\"-\\\", 1)[-1])\n    chunks = [(min(length, 35-low),low) for low in range(0,35,length)]\n    size = len(chunks)\n    impl = f\\\"\\\"\\\"\n  function automatic [34:0] segmented_subtract(\n    input logic [34:0] aa,\n    input logic [34:0] bb\n  );\n    logic [{size-2}:0] generate_borrow, propagate;\n    logic [{size-1}:0] borrow;\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    for idx,(width,offset) in enumerate(chunks):\n        impl += f\\\"    logic [{width}:0] diff_{idx};\\\\n\\\"\n    impl += \\\"    begin\\\\n      borrow[0] = 1'b0;\\\\n\\\"\n    for idx,(width,offset) in enumerate(chunks[:-1]):\n        impl += f\\\"      generate_borrow[{idx}] = aa[{offset} +: {width}] < bb[{offset} +: {width}];\\\\n\\\"\n        impl += f\\\"      propagate[{idx}] = aa[{offset} +: {width}] == bb[{offset} +: {width}];\\\\n\\\"\n        terms = []\n        for n in range(idx,-1,-1):\n            terms.append(\\\"(\\\"+\\\" && \\\".join([f\\\"generate_borrow[{n}]\\\",*(f\\\"propagate[{i}]\\\" for i in range(n+1,idx+1))])+\\\")\\\")\n        impl += f\\\"      borrow[{idx+1}] = \\\"+\\\" || \\\".join(terms)+\\\";\\\\n\\\"\n    for idx,(width,offset) in enumerate(chunks):\n        impl += f\\\"      diff_{idx} = {{aa[{offset} +: {width}], 1'b0}} - {{bb[{offset} +: {width}], borrow[{idx}]}};\\\\n\\\"\n        impl += f\\\"      segmented_subtract[{offset} +: {width}] = diff_{idx}[{width}:1];\\\\n\\\"\n    impl += \\\"    end\\\\n  endfunction\\\\n\\\"\n    alu = alu.replace(\\\"  function automatic [63:0] radix4_step(\\\", impl + \\\"\\\\n  function automatic [63:0] radix4_step(\\\")\n    for n,term in [(\\\"one\\\",\\\"{3'b0, divisor}\\\"),(\\\"two\\\",\\\"{2'b0, divisor, 1'b0}\\\"),(\\\"three\\\",\\\"{1'b0, triple_divisor}\\\")]:\n        alu = alu.replace(f\\\"shifted - {term};\\\",f\\\"segmented_subtract(shifted, {term});\\\")\nelse:\n    raise RuntimeError(sys.argv[1])\nalu_path.write_text(alu)\nPY\nfor variant in div-radix16 div-seg-8 div-seg-12; do python /srv/hwebench/tmp/7cb5c576/6b2b6527/bench_experiment.py \\\"\"'$variant\" || exit; done'", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
