{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\na=[json.loads(x) for x in Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines()]\nprint(a[-1].keys())\nfor x in a:\n if x['id'].endswith(('r1s0','r3s0','r4s0','r4s1','r7s0','r8s0','r9s1','r10s0','r10s1','r10s2','r11s0','r11s2')):\n  print('\\\\n',x['id'])\n  for k,v in x.items():\n   if k in ('title','motivation','hypothesis','notes','implementation_notes') or 'path' in k or 'timing' in k: print(k, str(v)[:2500])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\n\n hyp-20261119-001-r1s0\ntitle Use a shared six-round divider in execute\nmotivation The 5.442 MHz baseline has a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding,\nexecute and the ALU into the timed data-memory logic. The ALU infers\ncombinational division and remainder for both signed and unsigned inputs,\nmaking them the leading suspect for the long ALU path. The baseline\nVerilator retirement trace reproduced all 4,491,485 marker-bracketed\ncycles with both bus stalls active and contained zero DIV or REM family\ninstructions inside that window. Both DIVU retirements were outside it.\nSharing and registering division can cut ALU delay and area while adding\nexecution cycles only to those four operations.\n\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'The 5.442 MHz baseline has a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding,\\nexecute and the ALU into the timed data-memory logic. The ALU infers\\ncombinational division and remainder for both signed and unsigned inputs,\\nmaking them the leading suspect for the long ALU path. The baseline\\nVerilator retirement trace reproduced all 4,491,485 marker-bracketed\\ncycles with both bus stalls active and contained zero DIV or REM family\\ninstructions inside that window. Both DIVU retirements were outside it.\\nSharing and registering division can cut ALU delay and area while adding\\nexecution cycles only to those four operations.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"In the existing EX stage, capture the forwarded operands and run one unsigned\\nrestoring divider for six cycles of six radix-2 steps each. Prepend four\\nzero bits to the 32-bit dividend magnitude so every round can reuse the\\nsame datapath. Each step shifts a div\n…[57414 of 60486 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:090905f719bb06d3]…\ndecodes the slot in parallel and selects one bit from each of the existing sources before the same-bank bypass. This was a timing change to the slot selector. The replay reset, FENCE.I, stall, and collision behavior is preserved. Cocotb now checks recovery during clear and committed prediction during a pending same-index replacement. Tests that depend on a trained entry hold the first imem response through the clear.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint and all five cocotb suites passed.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retirement checks on the final RTL with zero failures and zero retries.\n- Co-simulation passed for five ELFs. Stalled CoreMark reported all five canonical CRCs and `Correct operation validated.` in 3,202,739 bracketed cycles.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 78.287, 79.456, and 79.456 MHz. The 79.456 MHz median projects 248.09 iterations/s and falls below the 90.75 MHz qualification threshold. The divider recurrence was the worst path in all three placements.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
