{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat formal/checks_si.cfg && cat fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv && sed -n '1,200p' fpga/core_bench_si.sv\"", "aggregated_output": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n// fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\n//\n// Memory-ready generator for the timed FPGA wrapper (HWE Bench V2).\n//\n// It reproduces, cycle for cycle, the bus backpressure that\n// test/cosim/main.cpp applies when CoreMark is run for fitness\n// (--istall --dstall): an xorshift32 seeded with 0xDEADBEEF, advanced\n// twice per cycle (first draw -> imem ready, second draw -> dmem ready),\n// accepting when (state & 0x7F) < 100.\n//\n// Why it exists: in V1 the wrapper tied both ready signals to 1, so\n// synthesis deleted any core logic that only acts while a ready is low.\n// That logic then saved simulated cycles at n\n…[4306 of 7378 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:df4adc4507dc1ae3]…\nde_0     (rvfi_mode_0),\n    .io_rvfi_ixl_0      (rvfi_ixl_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs1_addr_0 (rvfi_rs1_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_0(rvfi_rs1_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs2_addr_0 (rvfi_rs2_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_0(rvfi_rs2_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rd_addr_0  (rvfi_rd_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0 (rvfi_rd_wdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_pc_rdata_0 (rvfi_pc_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0 (rvfi_pc_wdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_addr_0 (rvfi_mem_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_rmask_0(rvfi_mem_rmask_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_wmask_0(rvfi_mem_wmask_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_rdata_0(rvfi_mem_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_wdata_0(rvfi_mem_wdata_0)\n  );\n\n  // V2: observe only the memory-side outputs. Everything the core computes\n  // reaches the fetch address or a store, so the datapath stays in the\n  // netlist; logic that only drives RVFI (a verification port a deployed\n  // core would not have) is pruned and does not count toward Fmax or area.\n  assign led = ^{imem_addr, dmem_addr, dmem_wdata, dmem_wen, dmem_ren, dmem_rdata};\n\nendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
