{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines():\n    row = json.loads(line)\n    print({k:row.get(k) for k in (\\\"id\\\",\\\"category\\\",\\\"fitness\\\",\\\"fmax_mhz\\\",\\\"cycles\\\",\\\"iterations\\\",\\\"lut4\\\",\\\"ff\\\")})\n    if row.get(\\\"category\\\") == \\\"micro_opt\\\" or row[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20261119-003-r2s2\\\":\n        print(row.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"))\n        for key in row:\n            if \\\"timing\\\" in key or \\\"path\\\" in key:\n                print(key,str(row[key])[:4500])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'id': 'baseline-bench-fe54f00', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'fitness': 12.12, 'fmax_mhz': 5.442, 'cycles': 4491485, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 12312, 'ff': 460}\n\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261119-001-r1s0', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'fitness': 93.78, 'fmax_mhz': 42.123, 'cycles': 4491485, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 2773, 'ff': 565}\n# Shared six-round divider\n\nThe EX ALU now shares one unsigned restoring divider across DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU. It captures the forwarded operands, runs six rounds of six radix-2 steps, and transfers the result on the eighth EX cycle when MEM can advance. The divider registers the partial remainder and reuses a 36-bit shift register for the padded dividend and outgoing quotient bits. ALTOPS captures the existing stand-in result and uses the same handshake and latency.\n\nThe divider derives signed results from unsigned magnitudes. A zero divisor naturally leaves the dividend magnitude in the remainder and produces an all-ones quotient. Sign restoration preserves the original dividend for a zero-divisor remainder and skips quotient negation in that case. The 32-bit magnitude and result also preserve `INT_MIN / -1` and its zero remainder.\n\nFetch and decode hold while EX waits. When MEM advances during the divide, EX/MEM captures a bubble with inactive controls, letting older instructions retire. A divide captures its forwarded values for RVFI at issue and passes through EX/MEM once, where the usual bypass serves the next instruction. The core retains its single-channel RVFI interface.\n\nA guarded include brings the core-wide types into scope for the requested alphabetical Verilator glob. Fetch flush is driven independently of the load-use check to remove Verilator's apparent feedback path in VPI builds.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Strict Verilator lint passed in hardware and ALTOPS modes.\n- `R\n…[5417 of 8489 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9470bcfd89cd103e]…\n payload is absent from the worst setup paths. The median options are limited by the five-step divider update from `partial_q_31_s1` to `partial_q_44_s0`, with a 25.649 ns arrival time. Regfile-to-data-memory paths follow closely. The small margin makes the measured gain sensitive to placement.\n\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_31_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_37_s0', 'slack_ns': -16.046, 'arrival_ns': 26.34, 'logic_cells': 150, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261119-002-r2s1', 'category': 'structural', 'fitness': 111.03, 'fmax_mhz': 48.337, 'cycles': 4353657, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 2819, 'ff': 627}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261119-003-r2s2', 'category': 'predictor', 'fitness': 114.06, 'fmax_mhz': 47.807, 'cycles': 4191341, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 3030, 'ff': 659}\n\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_34_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_35_s0', 'slack_ns': -16.108, 'arrival_ns': 26.403, 'logic_cells': 154, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
