{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r.get(\\\"id\\\") in [\\\"hyp-20261119-002-r1s1\\\",\\\"hyp-20261119-002-r2s1\\\",\\\"hyp-20261119-003-r2s2\\\"]:\n  print(r.keys())\n  print(r[\\\"id\\\"], r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\"), r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"),r.get(\\\"critical_path\\\"), sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id'])\nhyp-20261119-002-r1s1\n{'motivation': 'The bench retest reaches 5.442 MHz and reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through EX forwarding and the ALU to the data-memory path. The ALU feeds its common result mux with four combinational division and remainder expressions. The depth of an unrolled divider makes it the leading suspect for the low clock rate, and the mux exposes its delay even on cycles issuing ordinary instructions. A baseline Verilator retirement trace with both bus stalls enabled and all CoreMark CRCs validated counted zero DIV/REM instructions and 93,960 MUL instructions in the 4,491,485-cycle timed interval.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Replace the four combinational DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU implementations with one blocking, registered divider in EX. On launch, capture operand magnitudes and sign controls, then compute 32 quotient bits over seven registered restoring-division updates, with two bit steps in the first update and five in each of the next six. Each step shifts in one dividend bit, uses a 33-bit trial subtract to choose the next partial remainder, and appends the corresponding quotient bit. Select the quotient or remainder after the last update, apply the appropriate sign for signed operations, and transfer it through the usual EX/MEM boundary. Handle zero divisors and INT_MIN divided by -1 with their exact RV32M results on the same schedule. Keep multiply and RV32I on the single-cycle ALU path so matrix multiplication, address generation and ordinary dependencies incur no new EX latency.\\n\\nLaunch once from a valid divide/remainder in ID/EX when the older memory stage can advance. Hold IF and ID/EX during t\n…[13876 of 16948 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:22ff837751f2273f]…\ntion': 'Resolve full-width successor matches in parallel with branch direction, drive recovery and qualified BTB learning, and suppress architectural effects of invalid slots.'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Separate older-stage holds from younger-slot invalidation. Detect load-use hazards from ready raw fetches and keep redirect out of the data-memory hold logic.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect fetch PC, predictor metadata, EX feedback and pipeline validity while preserving the memory and single-channel RVFI ports.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise prediction hits, direction and target changes, same-index updates, misaligned control transfers and recovery across simultaneous iBus and dBus backpressure. Check RVFI order and exactly-once memory effects.'}]}\n\n{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_34_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_35_s0', 'slack_ns': -16.108, 'arrival_ns': 26.403, 'logic_cells': 154, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
