{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d = json.loads(line)\n if not any(s in d['id'] for s in ('r4s0','r4s1','r5s0','r6s0','r6s1','r6s2')): continue\n print(d['id'], d['fmax_mhz'], d['cycles'],d.get('seeds'), d.get('critical_path'))\n print('NOTES', d.get('implementation_notes', ''))\n print()\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-001-r4s0 60.126 4227639 [58.616, 60.126, 60.126] {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/btb_valid_5_s0', 'slack_ns': -12.06, 'arrival_ns': 22.355, 'logic_cells': 43, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']}\nNOTES \n\nhyp-20261119-002-r4s1 61.972 3987921 [62.201, 61.972, 61.972] {'from': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/pc_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -11.077, 'arrival_ns': 21.371, 'logic_cells': 29, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_mem', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']}\nNOTES # Execute forwarding in cores/bench\n\nID registers source matches against the instructions advancing from EX and MEM. EX qualifies the matches with the producers' write controls and selects from the ALU and jump-link lane, multiply lane, formatted memory response, MEM/WB value, or captured register-file value. The youngest eligible writer wins. The x0 comparisons are suppressed, and a misaligned load leaves a matching older writer eligible.\n\nThe core's ALU takes raw forwarded register operands for its signed 33-by-33 product. It selects the low or high half before EX/MEM. The ALTOPS formulas use the same lane, and the standalone ALU still returns multiply results on its default output.\n\nMEM selects load bytes and sign bits in parallel, then registers one value for writeback and the older bypass. A pending data request holds ID/EX and EX/MEM. MEM/WB clears retirement validity while retaining its forwarding value and writer qualification. A ready load and its immediate consumer advance together. Misaligned accesses raise the trap without issuing a data request or waiting for bus readiness.\n\n## Divider timing\n\nThe first placement sweep measured 52.765 MHz median and put the divider recurrence on the critical path. The final divider processes the leading six dividend bits with narrow logic on its first update, then four bits per update for six updates. The last radix-4 digit resolves from the held state in the completion phase. DIV and REM remain on the ordinary lane and use the original launch, completion, and \n…[8525 of 11597 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6cc90e12bf964e85]…\nigns for every byte and halfword position, and a taken misaligned branch hitting an existing BTB entry.\n- Full RVFI co-simulation passed on selftest and all three random programs with and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark matched the five canonical CRCs in **3,987,921 marker-bracketed cycles** for 10 iterations.\n\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax (MHz) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 71.789 |\n| 1 | 73.329 |\n| 2 | 73.329 |\n\nOption 0 used 3,342 logic cells and 887 registers. The 73.329 MHz median gives **183.88 CoreMark iterations/s**, up **8.70%** from 169.16. The worst option-0 path runs from data RAM to the registered BTB counter. Options 1 and 2 are limited by the path from the registered taken decision to the IF next-PC register.\n\n\nhyp-20261119-003-r6s2 64.781 3561615 [62.837, 64.781, 64.781] {'from': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_20_s0', 'slack_ns': -10.914, 'arrival_ns': 21.209, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_mem', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nNOTES \n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
