{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_86", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat formal/checks_si.cfg && rg -n 'DIV|REM|divide' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py cores/bench/test/test_alu.py | head -65\"", "aggregated_output": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:1:\"\"\"Check combinational ALU results and the registered divider handshake.\"\"\"\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:14:    ALU_DIV, ALU_DIVU, ALU_REM, ALU_REMU,\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:19:DIV_UPDATES = 7\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:63:    for update in range(1, DIV_UPDATES + 1):\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:66:        assert int(dut.div_valid.value) == (update == DIV_UPDATES), (\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:193:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIV, 10, 3, 3)\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:194:    await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIV, 0xFFFFFFFC, 2, 0xFFFFFFFE)      # -4/2 = -2\ncores\n…[3338 of 6410 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:15350c7877389b8d]…\nlse quotient\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:6:SW+LW roundtrip, load-response bypass, blocking divides, and trap discipline.\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:61:def DIV (rd, rs1, rs2): return _r(1, rs2, rs1, 0b100, rd, 0b0110011)\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:62:def DIVU(rd, rs1, rs2): return _r(1, rs2, rs1, 0b101, rd, 0b0110011)\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:63:def REMU(rd, rs1, rs2): return _r(1, rs2, rs1, 0b111, rd, 0b0110011)\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:440:async def divide_waits_for_stalled_store_and_forwards(dut):\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:445:        DIV(3, 1, 2),\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:472:async def load_to_divide_retirement_gap(dut, stall_cycles):\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:473:    program = [ADDI(2, 0, 6), LW(1, 0, 0x40), DIVU(3, 1, 2), REMU(4, 3, 2),\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:480:    # The ready load response feeds divider launch on the same edge.\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:711:@cocotb.parametrize(wrong_path=[DIVU(6, 3, 3), SW(3, 0, 0x48)])\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
