{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor n, line in enumerate(open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'), 1):\n    d=json.loads(line)\n    if n in [6,10,15,16,22,24,25,26,28]:\n        print(n, d['id'],d.get('title'),d.get('fitness'), d.get('cycles'),d.get('critical_path'))\n        print(d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "6 hyp-20261119-002-r2s1 Decouple fetch with one fall-through instruction slot 111.03 4353657 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -16.4, 'arrival_ns': 26.695, 'logic_cells': 16, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n\n10 hyp-20261119-003-r3s2 Run the BTB ahead of decode across predicted control transfers 124.01 3959069 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -15.717, 'arrival_ns': 26.012, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n# Implementation notes\n\nThe 32-entry BTB drives a request PC that follows the chosen successor on each accepted instruction response. A four-entry fall-through FIFO holds the full PC, instruction, and recorded successor. ID can bypass the empty queue or consume its fixed head while imem is unready. Load-use, dmem, and divider stalls constrain ID issue, and fetch can fill all four entries during those stalls. A full queue can dequeue and refill on the same edge.\n\nThe instruction's recorded successor goes through ID/EX. EX compares it with the full-width target and `PC + 4` in parallel with direction resolution. A mismatch or an advancing FENCE.I flushes the queue and squashes the younger ID/EX slot. RVFI reports the resolved architectural successor. At `0x000F_FFFC`, a sequential prediction holds the request and marks bit zero of the saved successor. EX's normal recovery clears the hold and supplies the full architectural address.\n\nID calculates `PC + 4` from the selected head PC and latches a one-bit FENCE.I decode for EX. Registering that decode reduced the timed instruction bits carried into EX by nine. BTB tag and counter metadata have a separate read by the head PC, including the same-index EX update bypass. The target array is read by the request PC. EX qualifies training and recovery with instruction advance. FIFO occupancy determines validity after a flush, and only occupied entries shift on a dequeue.\n\nD\n…[15434 of 18506 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b0625b8208acfbb3]…\n\n  passed, including the 50 pipeline cases.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 checks with the configured\n  single-retire wrapper and zero retries. The bounded formal checks\n  cover bus operation during startup. The directed pipeline tests\n  exercise replay at and after scrub completion.\n- Co-simulation matched selftest and all three random programs against\n  the reference with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark produced the\n  canonical CRCs and validated operation.\n- Gowin mapped replay to 10 BSRAMs. Option 0 used 3,448 logic cells,\n  926 registers, and 14 BSRAMs total. Placement options 0, 1, and 2\n  reached 66.153, 68.560, and 68.560 MHz, respectively. Option 0 was\n  limited by EX recovery to the replay read address. Options 1 and 2\n  were limited by data RAM to the EX shifter.\n- CoreMark took 3,183,041 marker-bracketed cycles across 10 iterations,\n  9,068 fewer cycles than the champion. The 68.560 MHz median yields\n  215.39 iterations/s and is 8.910 MHz below the 77.47 MHz promotion\n  threshold.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
