{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'r10s2|r11s[012]|r1s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n a=json.loads(l); print(a[\\\"id\\\"],a[\\\"title\\\"],a[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"],a[\\\"fitness\\\"],a[\\\"cycles\\\"]); print(a[\\\"seeds\\\"]); print(a[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"][:6000] if a[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"] else \\\"\\\"); print()'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-002-r1s1 Share a registered execute-stage divider for DIV and REM 46.963 104.56 4491485\n[44.54, 46.963, 46.963]\n\n\nhyp-20261119-003-r10s2 Select the BTB and recovery successors in parallel 86.757 270.88 3202739\n[76.343, 86.757, 86.757]\n# Bench IF successor selection\n\n`cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv` selects eight full-width next-PC sources with one masked OR. Ordinary fetch selects the held PC, PC+4, the committed BTB target, or the pending target write. Taken and fall-through recovery each select the corrected PC or its precomputed increment. The selector feeds the PC register and both synchronous replay lookups.\n\nThe committed and pending BTB tag checks feed separate target enables. The two-bit counter decisions and the ID metadata repair follow the existing training rules. Recovery takes precedence and uses instruction-bus readiness and the MEM hold to determine acceptance. Last-word parking and reset participate in the source enables. The existing FENCE.I invalidation, replay collision handling, and full-width EX validation still apply.\n\nThe timing-driven refinements qualify the ordinary paths in parallel with word availability and express the final mask as a per-bit reduction. Replay selects the requested slot bit from both bitmap sources before applying the existing same-bank bypass. The remaining hit qualifiers settle in parallel with slot selection.\n\n## Timing and throughput\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 76.343, 86.757, and 86.757 MHz. A repeat from the final worktree reproduced all three values. The 86.757 MHz median exceeds the 84.13 MHz promotion threshold. CoreMark completed 10 iterations in 3,202,739 marker-bracketed cycles with all canonical CRCs and the validation message. This projects 270.88 iterations per second, 7.87% above the champion at the same cycle count.\n\nThe two median placements are limited by the registered dependency match through the EX target comparison. Bitmap-to-replay address, divider recurrence, and replay-to-register-file paths are nearly tied. Option \n…[5114 of 8186 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4c2584601d582c02]…\necodes the slot in parallel and selects one bit from each of the existing sources before the same-bank bypass. This was a timing change to the slot selector. The replay reset, FENCE.I, stall, and collision behavior is preserved. Cocotb now checks recovery during clear and committed prediction during a pending same-index replacement. Tests that depend on a trained entry hold the first imem response through the clear.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint and all five cocotb suites passed.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retirement checks on the final RTL with zero failures and zero retries.\n- Co-simulation passed for five ELFs. Stalled CoreMark reported all five canonical CRCs and `Correct operation validated.` in 3,202,739 bracketed cycles.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 78.287, 79.456, and 79.456 MHz. The 79.456 MHz median projects 248.09 iterations/s and falls below the 90.75 MHz qualification threshold. The divider recurrence was the worst path in all three placements.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
