{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md && rg -n 'structural|divider' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r1s0 (regression, +673.76%): Replacing combinational DIV/REM with a shared, registered restoring divider moved the critical path from EX-to-memory logic into the six-step divider round, raising median Gowin Fmax from 5.442 to 42.123 MHz while the divide-free CoreMark window avoided the extra EX cycles.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.09%): With combinational DIV/REM in EX still limiting the clock to 5.5 MHz, the 16-entry tagged BTB's 6.1% CoreMark cycle savings from reusing taken branch and jump targets under bus stalls were too small to close the throughput gap to the 47.0 MHz registered-divider variant.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-001-r2s0 (regression, +4.61%): Squashing decode through the ID/EX valid bit cut the EX redirect feedback through IF and hazard logic into the ID/EX payload, exposing the five-step divider update as the Gowin timing limit and leaving a placement-sensitive CoreMark gain at 49.128 MHz median Fmax with unchanged cycle count.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-002-r2s1 (regression, +6.19%): A one-entry fall-through fetch slot cut CoreMark cycles by 3.07% by saving ready imem responses during decode holds, while the round's BTB won at a lower median Fmax by avoiding taken-branch and jump bubbles and cutting cycles by 6.68%.\n- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r2s2 (improvement, +9.09%): To pair the BTB's CoreMark cycle savings under bus stalls with a shorter recovery path, precompute full-width direct targets in ID, compare the fetch PC against target and fall-through in parallel with branch resolution, and redirect fetch with a validity-only ID/EX squash.\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261119-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Use a shared six-round divider in execute\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The 5.442 MHz baseline has a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding,\\nexecute and the ALU into the timed data-memory logic. The ALU infers\\ncombinational division and remainder for both signed and unsigned inputs,\\nmaking them the leading suspect for the long ALU path. The ba\n…[55330 of 58402 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cd88637ead3ab790]…\n6, \"delta_pct\": 9.09, \"vs_baseline\": 841.09, \"fmax_mhz\": 47.807, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4191341, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3030, \"ff\": 659, \"seeds\": [47.375, 47.807, 47.807], \"perturbations\": [[0, 47.375, 31], [1, 47.807, 31], [2, 47.807, 31]], \"lutram\": 26, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_34_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_35_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -16.108, \"arrival_ns\": 26.403, \"logic_cells\": 154, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 31, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-19T14:53:04.326426Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-19 hyp-20261119-003-r2s2 (improvement, +9.09%): To pair the BTB's CoreMark cycle savings under bus stalls with a shorter recovery path, precompute full-width direct targets in ID, compare the fetch PC against target and fall-through in parallel with branch resolution, and redirect fetch with a validity-only ID/EX squash.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
