{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n    d=json.loads(line)\n    if d['category']=='structural' or d['id'].startswith('hyp-20261119-00') and ('r5' in d['id'] or '001-r4' in d['id']):\n        print(d['id'], d['title'], d['fitness'], d['fmax_mhz'], d['cycles'])\n        print(d['critical_path'])\n        print(d['implementation_notes'][:4200] if isinstance(d['implementation_notes'],str) else d['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-002-r1s1 Share a registered execute-stage divider for DIV and REM 104.56 46.963 4491485\n{'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_addr_1_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.is_jalr_s0', 'slack_ns': -17.452, 'arrival_ns': 27.746, 'logic_cells': 54, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id']}\n\nhyp-20261119-002-r2s1 Decouple fetch with one fall-through instruction slot 111.03 48.337 4353657\n{'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -16.4, 'arrival_ns': 26.695, 'logic_cells': 16, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n\nhyp-20261119-002-r3s1 Split the address path for bubble-free load forwarding 122.55 48.871 3987921\n{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_32_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_33_s0', 'slack_ns': -16.163, 'arrival_ns': 26.457, 'logic_cells': 162, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\n\nhyp-20261119-001-r4s0 Split RV32M arithmetic across existing register boundaries 142.22 60.126 4227639\n{'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/btb_valid_5_s0', 'slack_ns': -12.06, 'arrival_ns': 22.355, 'logic_cells': 43, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']}\n\nhyp-20261119-002-r4s1 Split execute forwarding into ALU, multiply and load lanes 155.4 61.972 3987921\n{'from': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/pc_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -11.077, 'arrival_ns': 21.371, 'logic_cells': 29, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_mem', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']}\n# Execute forwarding in cores/bench\n\nID registers source matches against the instructions advancing from EX and MEM. EX qualifies the matches with the producers' write controls and selects from the ALU and jump-link lane, multiply lane, formatted memory response, MEM/WB value, or captured register-file value. The youngest eligible writer wins. The x0 comparisons are suppressed, and a misaligned load leaves a matching older writer eligible.\n\nThe core's ALU takes raw forwarded register operands for its signed 33-by-33 product.\n…[7211 of 10283 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b585032d83f8ba84]…\nhe requested source list.\n- `formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retire ALTOPS checks, including liveness. No counterexamples or formal fix retries were needed.\n- All five cocotb runners passed, including 36 pipeline cases. The directed cases cover one-cycle ready recovery, consecutive prediction hits, same-index writes, JALR target changes and traps, divider suppression, bus-stall retry, FENCE.I, and last-word parking.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` passed full RVFI reference comparison for selftest and three random programs with and without bus stalls. CoreMark passed all five canonical CRCs with both stall streams.\n- `make fpga TARGET=bench` reproduced 3,988,962 marker-bracketed cycles for 10 CoreMark iterations. Median Fmax was 65.503 MHz, above the 64.84 MHz floor. The resulting 164.21 iter/s is 5.67% above 155.40 iter/s.\n\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax (MHz) | Logic cells | Registers |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 0 | 64.555 | 3,538 | 880 |\n| 1 | 65.503 | 3,538 | 880 |\n| 2 | 65.503 | 3,538 | 880 |\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
