e selected successor mismatched\\nand otherwise present the normal request. Use that presented PC\\nthroughout IF, including lookup, hold, and the next EX comparison.\\nUse mutually exclusive normal, taken-target and fall-through\\nselections after the registers to keep the late EX predicates\\noff the wide IF PC register input mux.\\n\\nCapture ID/EX payload and candidate validity independently of the\\ncurrent EX decision. Mask the younger slot with the registered\\nmismatch before it can launch the di\n…[33653 of 36725 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5dcb640a536efcd6]…\nessor validation separately from imem readiness and address generation. Preserve the memory and nret=1 RVFI ports.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Capture the selected logical fetch word, decode FENCE.I for frontend invalidation, and keep existing validity masking independent of payload capture.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Validate the logical successor at the existing registered boundary, emit a one-shot qualified training record, and force refetch on an advancing FENCE.I. Preserve forwarding, traps and architectural next PC.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise two-word replay during imem stalls, FENCE.I refetch and last-word recovery. Check recovery and JALR address sequences at the logical issue PC. Exercise consecutive counter updates with a stable self-loop and check saturation, and cache real store and divide opcodes before testing their wrong-path suppression across a dmem hold. Preserve forwarding, trap and ordered RVFI assertions.'}]}\nNone\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
