{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261119-(003-r5s2|002-r5s1|002-r6s1)\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n r=json.loads(l)\n print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"]); print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"][:3700]); print(str(r[\\\"critical_path\\\"])[:420])'\n\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-002-r5s1 Retime fetch recovery across the execute boundary\nAt the existing EX/MEM edge, register the advancing instruction's\ntarget, fall-through PC, aligned-taken predicate, and the separate\nfull-width target and fall-through matches against this cycle's\npresented fetch PC. Register a one-cycle resolution-valid bit that\naccounts for EX validity, divide completion and MEM backpressure.\nIF independently registers its normal next request, choosing its\nBTB or sequential successor on fetch advance and the currently\npresented address on hold. From the registered predicates,\nselect the resolved address when the selected successor mismatched\nand otherwise present the normal request. Use that presented PC\nthroughout IF, including lookup, hold, and the next EX comparison.\nUse mutually exclusive normal, taken-target and fall-through\nselections after the registers to keep the late EX predicates\noff the wide IF PC register input mux.\n\nCapture ID/EX payload and candidate validity independently of the\ncurrent EX decision. Mask the younger slot with the registered\nmismatch before it can launch the divider, issue, or train the\nBTB. If ID/EX holds when the mask is asserted, clear the stored\ncandidate validity on that edge so the killed slot cannot reappear.\nThe resolution record expires after one cycle even if dmem stalls.\nCarry the corrected presented address forward on an imem hold.\nThe advancing older instruction, including its resolved RVFI PC\nand any memory effects, follows the existing in-order path.\n\nStage BTB training at the same boundary. Overlay the pending\nregistered update on the lookup for the same index before the\nphysical write edge so direction and target are visible on the\noriginal cycle. Overlay target, tag and valid only for a target\nwrite. Overlay the counter on every counter write. At ID/EX,\napply the pending update to the saved predictor metadata when\nits index matches, checking tag and range and treating a replacement\ntag as a miss. Save that repaired metadata if the candidate holds\npast the up\n…[7034 of 10106 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c5efbc3c7989c40c]…\ninvalid writer controls, and preserve the current\ndivide launch, completion and consume schedule in hardware and\nALTOPS. Keep one in-order RVFI retirement stream.\n\nA scratch implementation measured 70.068, 72.388 and 72.388 MHz\nacross Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2, using 3,341 logic cells and\n940 registers in option 0. Stalled CoreMark matched the canonical CRCs\nin 3,987,921 marker-bracketed cycles, giving 181.52 iter/s. The gain is\n7.3% over 169.16, clearing the 4.6% acceptance margin. The median\nplacements were limited by register-file readback into the multiply\nresult. The scratch RTL passed all 53 single-retire ALTOPS checks,\nall five cocotb suites, and full RVFI co-simulation on selftest and\nall three random programs with and without bus stalls. Reproduce the\nthree placements, bracketed cycles and existing gates on implementation.\n\n{'from': 'dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/train_counter_q_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -8.93, 'arrival_ns': 19.224, 'logic_cells': 15, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
