{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nls=[json.loads(x) for x in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nprint(ls[-1].keys())\nfor v in ls[-5:]:\n print('\\\\n',v['id'],v['title']); print({k:x for k,x in v.items() if k in ['metrics','result','fitness','implementation_notes','notes','outcome','baseline_fitness'] and k not in ['metrics','result']}); print({k:list(x) if isinstance(x,dict) else x for k,x in v.items() if k in ['metrics','result']})\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\n\n hyp-20261119-002-r7s1 Route immediate load forwarding through branch and address lanes\n{'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 197.9, 'implementation_notes': \"# Bench load forwarding\\n\\n- EX now gives branch comparisons, effective addresses and store data the formatted MEM response through the existing one-hot forwarding selectors. The ALU, multiplier, divider and JALR adder receive only register-backed operands.\\n- ID predecodes a two-bit mask for the source operands that can require replay. On acceptance of a matching older load, EX inserts one bubble, and ID retains the other forwarded operand and retags each matching raw source for MEM/WB. Decode continues to capture both raw source fields for RVFI, including immediate bits in instruction fields the execution unit ignores.\\n- EX registers the byte comparisons, sign terms and branch controls for late recovery. The same comparison function resolves the issuing slot's RVFI PC and trap before the register. Jump link writes depend directly on target alignment. Both saturated BTB counter candidates are registered with the live training slot.\\n- IF uses three read ports on one logical BTB. Each request computes its own successor and applies the pending write with a tag check before recovery selects the request and metadata. The full-width successor checks and corrected-address retry remain in place.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Verilator `--lint-only -Wall` passed. All five cocotb suites passed, including 39 pipeline cases. Directed checks cover consecutive pointer-load, byte-load and signed-branch retirements, single-cycle ALU and JALR replay, divider launch timing, retai\n…[7727 of 10799 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0de428fbca2efb75]…\nand FENCE.I refetch, clear priority, and rearm.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\\n- `make test TARGET=bench` passed all five cocotb suites, including 49 pipeline cases.\\n- `formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retire ALTOPS checks on the final RTL. No formal fixes were needed.\\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed RVFI comparison for selftest and three random programs with and without bus stalls, plus stalled CoreMark CRC validation. The local build used explicit `NRET=1` to match `core.yaml`.\\n- `make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1` reproduced all three Gowin results at 71.145, 74.271, and 74.271 MHz. The median was 74.271 MHz. Option 0 used 5,249 logic cells, 1,935 registers, and seven BSRAMs. The worst setup paths crossed data RAM into the EX multiply or shift result registers.\\n- CoreMark completed in 3,192,109 marker-bracketed cycles with all expected CRCs and the UART validation message. The measured fitness was 232.67 iterations/s, up 9.33% from 212.81 iterations/s.\\n'}\n{}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
