{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_27", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat fpga/core_bench_si.sv | head -180; rg -n 'replay|btb|branch' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | head -120\"", "aggregated_output": "// fpga/core_bench_si.sv\n//\n// FPGA Fmax wrapper for single-issue (`nret 1`) cores. Same shape as\n// core_bench.sv but instantiates `core` with only the channel-0 RVFI port\n// set — no `_1` ports. Selected by the orchestrator (via BENCH env var in\n// synth.tcl) when cores/<target>/core.yaml declares nret: 1.\n//\n// See core_bench.sv for the rationale on LFSR-driven imem, the dmem\n// model, the V2 stall generator, and why the LED observes only the\n// memory-side outputs (RVFI-only logic is pruned).\nmodule core_bench (\n  input  logic clock,\n  input  logic reset,\n  output logic led\n);\n\n  logic [31:0] lfsr;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock or posedge reset)\n    if (reset) lfsr <= 32'h1;\n    else       lfsr <= {lfsr[30:0], lfsr[31] ^ lfsr[21] ^ lfsr[1] ^ lfsr[0]};\n\n  logic [31:0] dmem [0:2047];\n  logic [31:0] dmem_rdata;\n  logic [31:0] dmem_addr;\n  logic [31:0] dmem_wdata;\n  logic [3:0]  dmem_wen;\n  logic        dmem_ren;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (dmem_wen[0]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][7:0]   <= dmem_wdata[7:0];\n    if (dmem_wen[1]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][15:8]  <= dmem_wdata[15:8];\n    if (dmem_wen[2]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][23:16] <= dmem_wdata[23:16];\n    if (dmem_wen[3]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][31:24] <= dmem_wdata[31:24];\n  end\n  assign dmem_rdata = dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]];\n\n  logic [31:0] imem_addr;\n  // Single-channel RVFI port set (NRET=1 contract). Connected for\n  // elaboration only; nothing observes it, so synthesis prunes it.\n  logic        rvfi_valid_0;\n  logic [63:0] rvfi_order_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_insn_0, rvfi_pc_rdata_0, rvfi_pc_wdata_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_rd_wdata_0, rvfi_rs1_rdata_0, rvfi_rs2_rdata_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_mem_addr_0, rvfi_mem_rdata_0, rvfi_mem_wdata_0;\n  logic [4:0]  rvfi_rs1_addr_0, rvfi_rs2_addr_0, rvfi_rd_addr_0;\n  logic [3:0]  rvfi_mem_rmask_0, rvfi_mem_wmask_0;\n  logic [1:0]  rvfi_mode_0, rvfi_ixl_0;\n  logic        rvfi_trap_0, rvfi_halt_0, rvfi_intr_0;\n\n  // V2: memory-ready signals come from the same stall sequence the\n  // CoreMark simulation uses, so stall-handling logic\n…[3484 of 6556 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5a5651e86ba20cf1]…\ne\"] - rets[i][\"cycle\"] for i in branches] == [3, 1, 2, 2, 1]\n775:async def taken_misaligned_branch_does_not_train_on_hit(dut):\n777:    # Change the third visit into a taken branch with a misaligned target.\n901:async def target_replay_persists_and_refreshes_ready_words(dut):\n906:    branch = count_pc + 4\n912:        branch: BNE(1, 2, target - branch),\n913:        branch + 4: EBREAK(),\n924:        if pc == branch:\n930:    body = stream + [count_pc, branch]\n931:    _check_retirements(rets, [0, 4] + body * 3 + [branch + 4])\n938:    expected += [(count_pc, True, True), (branch, True, True)]\n945:async def target_replay_checks_full_tag(dut, tag_bit):\n947:    b = a + (1 << tag_bit)  # Same replay index, different tags.\n966:async def target_replay_read_while_filling(dut, spacing):\n1004:async def fence_i_invalidates_replay_and_refetches_younger_word(dut):\n1048:    # and the second jump replays the replacement with imem still stalled.\n1087:    # taken entry. The fallthrough stays out of replay until a later taken edge.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261119-003-r[789]s2\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"motivation\\\"],x[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"][:6500]) for x in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_28", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261119-003-r[789]s2\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"motivation\\\"],x[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"][:6500]) for x in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-003-r7s2 The 32-entry BTB already predicts most CoreMark successors. The previous\ntwo-word target replay cut timed cycles by 10.69%, but its 64.781 MHz\nmedian left it below the 183.88 iter/s champion. A wider window covers\nmore recurrent target instructions. Reading the replay word one cycle\nahead gives the decoder a registered word and keeps the replay store off\nthe same-cycle path from EX recovery to the register file.\n # Read BTB target replay one fetch ahead\n\nIF reads a 128-word direct-mapped replay RAM at the same edge that registers the next ordinary fetch PC. Each entry stores PC[19:9] and the instruction. A resettable bitmap tracks validity. The registered fill strobe and index suppress a same-index hit on the following cycle, independent of the RAM's read-during-write mode.\n\nA taken BTB prediction or a taken EX correction starts a 32-word window. An accepted corrected word consumes its first slot. If that word selects another taken successor, the window starts at the newly selected target. Recovery drives the corrected address and requires a ready bus response for acceptance. When recovery holds, IF registers the corrected address and reads replay at that address. The instruction mux selects its payload using raw imem readiness. IF qualifies acceptance separately with the replay tag, range, validity, collision, and pipeline hold checks.\n\nThe IF logic now supplies word validity directly to ID. The hazard unit retains the data-memory and divider hold logic. EX carries a one-cycle FENCE.I refetch bit and ignores parked addresses in its successor comparisons. This lets a jump at the last RAM word recover even when it targets that same word. FENCE.I forces a fall-through refetch, clears replay validity, and cancels the old window.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\n- `formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retire ALTOPS checks. No counterexamples or correctness retries.\n- All five cocotb suites passed, including 38 pipeline cases. New cases cover 32 accepted words, rea\n…[6127 of 9199 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:393507d25777abcd]…\n\n  passed, including the 50 pipeline cases.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 checks with the configured\n  single-retire wrapper and zero retries. The bounded formal checks\n  cover bus operation during startup. The directed pipeline tests\n  exercise replay at and after scrub completion.\n- Co-simulation matched selftest and all three random programs against\n  the reference with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark produced the\n  canonical CRCs and validated operation.\n- Gowin mapped replay to 10 BSRAMs. Option 0 used 3,448 logic cells,\n  926 registers, and 14 BSRAMs total. Placement options 0, 1, and 2\n  reached 66.153, 68.560, and 68.560 MHz, respectively. Option 0 was\n  limited by EX recovery to the replay read address. Options 1 and 2\n  were limited by data RAM to the EX shifter.\n- CoreMark took 3,183,041 marker-bracketed cycles across 10 iterations,\n  9,068 fewer cycles than the champion. The 68.560 MHz median yields\n  215.39 iterations/s and is 8.910 MHz below the 77.47 MHz promotion\n  threshold.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'probe_dir=\"$TMPDIR/bench-predictor.YqPaFu\"\ncp -r cores/bench/rtl \"$probe_dir/profile_rtl\"\npython3 - \"$probe_dir/profile_rtl/core.sv\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(sys.argv[1]); s = p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('endmodule', '''  logic bench_profile_active;\n  always @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset)\n      bench_profile_active <= 0;\n    else begin\n      if (io_dmemReady && |io_dmemWEn) begin\n        if (io_dmemAddr == 32'h1000_0100)\n          bench_profile_active <= 1;\n        if (io_dmemAddr == 32'h1000_0104)\n          bench_profile_active <= 0;\n      end\n      if (bench_profile_active && fetch_resolution.valid && (ex_mem_w.ctrl.is_branch || ex_mem_w.ctrl.is_jump))\n        \"'$display(\"CF %x %x %x %b %b %b %b\", ex_mem_w.pc, ex_mem_w.instr, pc_next, squash_candidate,\n                 !io_imemReady, fetch_resolution.take_target, u_ex.train_target_q);\n    end\n  end\nendmodule'\"'''); p.write_text(s)\nPY\nOBJ_DIR=\\\"\"'$probe_dir/profile_sim\" RTL_DIR=\"$probe_dir/profile_rtl\" NRET=1 bash test/cosim/build.sh > \"$probe_dir/profile_sim.log\" 2>&1 && \"$probe_dir/profile_sim/cosim_sim\" \"$probe_dir/coremark.elf\" 50000000 --bench --istall --dstall > \"$probe_dir/profile.out\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
