{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'hyp-20261119-(00[123])-(r10s[012]|r11s2|r12s[012]|r9s2)' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; keys=\\\"id cycles fitness fmax_mhz ipc_coremark critical_path logic_levels lut4 ff bsram\\\".split(); [print(*(f\\\"{k}={d.get(k)}\\\" for k in keys),\\\"\\\\n\\\",d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\", \\\"\\\")[:2800],\\\"\\\\n\\\") for d in (json.loads(x.split(\\\":\\\",1)[1]) for x in sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "id=hyp-20261119-003-r9s2 cycles=3183041 fitness=215.39 fmax_mhz=68.56 ipc_coremark=3e-06 critical_path={'from': 'cpu/u_ex/fetch_resolution.valid_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/replay_entry_replay_entry_0_1_s', 'slack_ns': -10.116, 'arrival_ns': 20.411, 'logic_cells': 17, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_if']} logic_levels=13 lut4=3448 ff=926 bsram=14 \n # Bench replay RAM\n\n`if_stage.sv` uses a synchronous 4,096 × 39-bit replay RAM indexed by\nPC[13:2]. Each word packs validity, PC[19:14], and the instruction. The\nRAM reads from the same next-PC value that the ordinary fetch register\ncaptures. The next-PC mux uses one-hot selects for the predicted target,\nfall-through, and held PC. This improved the local median from 66.274 MHz\nwith the original mux to 68.560 MHz.\n\nReset and each advancing FENCE.I block replay immediately. The shared\nwrite port then clears validity at indices 0 through 4095, with the bus\ndriving the tag and instruction on every write. Invalidation restarts the\nsweep and clears the arm even when a taken prediction coincides with it.\nImem can supply instructions throughout the sweep. Taken predictions and\nrecoveries can arm replay during the sweep, and accepted ready imem words\nresume filling it after the final write. A sampled write strobe and\n12-bit index suppress the read/write collision, including the final\nscrub write. A ready bus response still supplies the accepted instruction\nand can refresh an existing replay word.\n\nThe pipeline tests warm the replay-specific fixtures and check bus\nretirement during a scrub, reset and consecutive FENCE.I restarts with\nimem backpressure, refill and replay after the scrub, stale-word\nsuppression at the last scrub index, tag mismatches on PC[19:14], and\nsimultaneous reads and fills at matching and distinct indices.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint completed without warnings. All five cocotb suites\n  passed, including the 50 pipeline cases.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 checks with the configured\n  single-retire wrapper and zero r\n…[16253 of 19325 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3703c6a3b005e8ea]…\nuses.\n- Stalled CoreMark validated all five CRCs without an out-of-bounds access. The start and stop markers were at cycles 12,468 and 3,215,207, giving 3,202,739 timed cycles.\n- The single-retirement `formal/run_all.sh` gate passed all 53 checks on the final RTL, including the depth-20 register-consistency check. It used `wrapper_si.sv` and `checks_si.cfg` in a scratch copy. No formal fixes were needed.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| RTL | Option 0 | Option 1 | Option 2 | Median Fmax | Logic cells |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Champion rerun | 76.343 MHz | 86.757 MHz | 86.757 MHz | 86.757 MHz | 4,393 |\n| Parallel carry checks | 76.896 MHz | 79.924 MHz | 79.924 MHz | 79.924 MHz | 4,342 |\n\nThe divider's partial-remainder feedback limits options 1 and 2. The fetch replay path limits option 0. At the measured cycle count the median gives 249.55 CoreMark iterations/s, 7.88% below the champion. The median also falls short of the supplied scratch result of 82.978 MHz and the 90.75 MHz promotion threshold.\n \n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
