{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"du -sh formal/riscv-formal/ formal/riscv-formal/checks formal/riscv-formal/insns && sed -n '1,90p' formal/checks_si.cfg && ls -l \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/predictor.ycL9kF\"/eda4/gowin_p*/gw.log && rg -n '\"'DEPTH' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/predictor.ycL9kF/gowin4/if_stage.sv\"'","aggregated_output":"394M\tformal/riscv-formal/\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2 7240 Nov 19 16:02 /srv/hwebench/tmp/7cb5c576/8b5867fd/predictor.ycL9kF/eda4/gowin_p0/gw.log\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2 7240 Nov 19 16:02 /srv/hwebench/tmp/7cb5c576/8b5867fd/predictor.ycL9kF/eda4/gowin_p1/gw.log\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2 7240 Nov 19 16:02 /srv/hwebench/tmp/7cb5c576/8b5867fd/predictor.ycL9kF/eda4/gowin_p2/gw.log\n19:  localparam int DEPTH = 4;\n20:  localparam int COUNT_WIDTH = $clog2(DEPTH+1);\n30:  packet_t fifo [DEPTH];\n63:  assign refill = imem_ready && (count < COUNT_WIDTH'(DEPTH) || consume_head);\n82:  for (genvar idx = 0; idx < DEPTH; idx++) begin : g_fifo\n83:    if (idx+1 < DEPTH) begin : g_shift\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
