{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"agent_message","text":"Wrote and schema-validated the predictor hypothesis [hyp-20261119-003-r4s2.yaml](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261119-003-r4s2-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r4s2.yaml).\n\nThe proposal lets the BTB fetch ahead into a four-entry queue and derives each predicted successor from the next queued PC or the current request PC. That saves 128 bits of queue storage compared with the prior design.\n\nThe scratch prototype reached **136.62 CoreMark iter/s**, up **7.47%** from the champion and above the 4.6% acceptance margin. It ran in **3,959,069 bracketed cycles** at **54.089 MHz** median Gowin Fmax. The packed-vector implementation passed all 53 single-retire formal checks, all five cocotb suites, and RVFI cosimulation."}}
