get when taken.\\nFor either jump opcode, store the last resolved target as strongly taken.\\nKeep sequential fetch on misses and on hits whose counter predicts\\nfall-through. This puts a tag check and a mux on the fetch PC path.\\n\\nApply the prediction only when IF/ID is accepted into ID/EX. During the\\nfollowing EX cycle, the fetch PC is already that instruction's predicted\\nsuccessor and holds there if an older data access stalls EX. On a valid\\nEX advance, compare that PC with the full resolved architectural next PC\\nfor every instruction. On a mismatch, redirect and squash the younger\\ninstruction, even when instruction memor\n…[36197 of 39269 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:696f5a08137e99bf]…\n and EX recovery to IF. Retain the single-channel RVFI and memory interfaces.'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': \"Determine load-use and ID issue from the selected packet's validity and instruction fields, including when an occupied queue serves ID while imem is unready.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': \"Capture the issued packet's successor and FENCE.I decode. Keep payload capture independent of the validity-only squash.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Validate the recorded prediction on EX advance and flush on a mismatch, an invalid prediction or an advancing FENCE.I. Preserve full-width recovery, architectural next PC, trap handling and qualified BTB updates.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Cover implicit-successor selection through occupancy transitions, training after a packet was fetched, boundary recovery and wrong-path side-effect suppression across bus stalls. Check ordered RVFI and exactly-once memory effects.'}]}\nimplementation_notes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
