{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261119-(003-r10s2|001-r11s0|001-r12s0|001-r13s0|002-r13s1|003-r13s2)' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in sys.stdin]; print(rows[0].keys());\nfor r in rows:\n print(); print(r.get(\\\"id\\\"), [(k, str(v)[:650]) for k,v in r.items() if k not in (\\\"id\\\", \\\"implementation_notes\\\")]); print(str(r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"))[:5000])'\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\n\nhyp-20261119-003-r10s2 [('title', 'Select the BTB and recovery successors in parallel'), ('category', 'predictor'), ('motivation', 'The champion runs 10 CoreMark iterations in 3,202,739 cycles at a median\\n80.427 MHz. Both median placements are limited by the IF path into the\\nreplay validity RAM. IF currently forms two full-width ordinary successors\\nfor the pending BTB training outcomes and then selects between them and the\\ncorrected successors. A profile counted about 59,000 control-flow\\ncorrections through the end marker. Doubling the BTB saved only 0.22%\\nof CoreMark cycles, so the opportunity is in the prediction-to-replay\\ntiming path.\\n'), ('hypothesis', '{\\'motivation\\': \\'The champion runs 10 CoreMark iterations in 3,202,739 cycles at a median\\\\n80.427 MHz. Both median placements are limited by the IF path into the\\\\nreplay validity RAM. IF currently forms two full-width ordinary successors\\\\nfor the pending BTB training outcomes and then selects between them and the\\\\ncorrected successors. A profile counted about 59,000 control-flow\\\\ncorrections through the end marker. Doubling the BTB saved only 0.22%\\\\nof CoreMark cycles, so the opportunity is in the prediction-to-replay\\\\ntiming path.\\\\n\\', \\'hypothesis\\': \"Form independent one-hot enables for eight next-PC sources. Ordinary fetch\\\\nchooses among the '), ('expected_impact', \"{'fitness_delta_pct': 1, 'confidence': 'low'}\"), ('changes', \"[{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Derive mutually exclusive final source enables from ordinary acceptance,\\\\npending BTB training, reset, recovery direction, corrected acceptance\\\\nand last-word parking.\n…[26378 of 29450 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:854d34748e7176fe]…\ned CoreMark run completed 10 iterations in 3,202,739 marker-bracketed cycles, the same as the champion. A temporary Verilator monitor counted 13,735 JALRs, 1,235 absent hints (8.99%), 747 mismatches among the 12,500 hints, and 58,391 total corrections. Zero absent hints had an actual target equal to the live fetch PC.\n- Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 reached 80.861, 80.100, and 80.100 MHz. The 80.100 MHz median yields 250.10 iterations/s, 7.67% below the champion and below the 90.75 MHz promotion threshold.\n- The first trial selected the BTB lane ahead of its ID subtractors. Option 0 reported a 12.691 ns data delay from EX's registered branch equality into an ID/EX expected operand. The final version moves lane selection after the subtractors. Its ID/EX expected operands and EX match do not appear as endpoints in the 25 reported worst setup paths for any placement. The final median is limited by replay validity feeding the next fetch PC (12.449 ns data delay). The divider result path limits option 0 (12.332 ns).\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
