{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys;\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n r=json.loads(line)\n print(r[\\\"id\\\"], r[\\\"title\\\"], r.get(\\\"cycles\\\"), r.get(\\\"fmax_mhz\\\")); c=r.get(\\\"critical_path\\\") or {}; print(c.get(\\\"from\\\"), \\\"->\\\", c.get(\\\"to\\\"));\n if r[\\\"id\\\"] in (\\\"hyp-20261119-002-r4s1\\\", \\\"hyp-20261119-001-r9s0\\\", \\\"hyp-20261119-001-r7s0\\\"): print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"])'\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-fe54f00 Baseline retest for cores/bench 4491485 5.442\ncpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0 -> dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\nhyp-20261119-001-r1s0 Use a shared six-round divider in execute 4491485 42.123\ncpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_2_s0 -> cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_11_s0\nhyp-20261119-001-r2s0 Squash decode through the ID/EX valid bit 4491485 49.128\ncpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_31_s1 -> cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_37_s0\nhyp-20261119-001-r3s0 Shorten EX arithmetic paths to the divider and data memory 4191341 53.281\ncpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0 -> cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_2_s0\nhyp-20261119-001-r4s0 Split RV32M arithmetic across existing register boundaries 4227639 60.126\ncpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s -> cpu/u_if/btb_valid_5_s0\nhyp-20261119-001-r5s0 Share one execute comparator between branches and SLT 3987921 61.529\ncpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s -> cpu/u_if/btb_counter_btb_counter_1_0_s\nhyp-20261119-001-r6s0 Move late EX output selection across EX/MEM 3987921 71.49\ndmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s -> cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_23_s0\nhyp-20261119-001-r7s0 Compute AUIPC in ID to remove the EX operand mux 3987921 78.576\ndmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s -> cpu/u_ex/reg_q.mul_result_9_s0\n{'motivation': 'The bench champion scores 183.88 CoreMark iterations per second at\\n73.329 MHz in 3,987,921 marker-bracketed cycles. In the median Gowin\\nplacements, the path from data RAM through load forwarding and the\\nAUIPC operand mux into the EX/MEM shifter register is within 0.001 ns\\nof the worst fetch-recovery path. Every instruction on the ordinary\\nALU operand A path passes through that mux. AUIPC can compute its\\nresult from the fetch PC and instruction bits before EX because its\\nimmediate has twelve zero low bits and uses no register operand.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"On the existing ID/EX payload capture edge, register the low 20 bits\\nof pc[31:12] + instr[31:12] alongside the PC. In EX, concatenate this\\nsum with the saved pc[11:0] to form the full modulo-2^32 AUIPC result.\\nDrive the ALU A input directly from forwarded rs1. Exclude AUIPC from\\nthe add/subtract result selector and p\n…[4418 of 7490 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1c1c1abe8dd9bc6d]…\n sign controls. Gate it separately for MEM/WB writeback.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Route the common formatted load word from MEM to EX and retain the existing per-source load selectors.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Resolve register-backed operands and ALU PC or immediate choices in parallel with the load response. Select the load at the last operand mux.'}]}\nhyp-20261119-001-r10s0 Select fetch successors with one-hot enables 3202739 83.372\ncpu/u_ex/u_alu/divisor_q_0_s0 -> cpu/u_ex/u_alu/partial_q_35_s1\nhyp-20261119-001-r11s0 Share carry-select byte sums for JALR target and match 3202739 80.275\ncpu/u_if/normal_pc_q_5_s0 -> cpu/u_if/normal_pc_q_6_s0\nhyp-20261119-001-r12s0 Specialize divider updates by divisor magnitude 3202739 77.313\ncpu/u_if/replay_entry_replay_entry_0_2_s -> cpu/u_if/replay_entry_replay_entry_0_2_s\nhyp-20261119-001-r13s0 Retain held replay words outside the RAM address path 3202739 86.156\ncpu/u_ex/reg_q.result_sel.div_s0 -> cpu/u_ex/reg_q.shift_result_18_s0\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261119-002-r4s1|hyp-20261119-002-r9s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(r[\\\"id\\\"], r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"], r[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"], sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\") for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261119-002-r4s1|hyp-20261119-002-r9s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(r[\\\"id\\\"], r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"], r[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"], sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\") for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-002-r4s1\nRegister the ordinary ALU or jump-link result and the multiply result as\nindependent EX/MEM lanes. Run multiply from the raw forwarded operands\nso the immediate and AUIPC selection is off its input path. Use one\nsigned 33-by-33 product, extending rs1 with its sign bit for MULH and\nMULHSU and rs2 with its sign bit for MULH. Use a zero extension otherwise.\nSelect bits 31:0 for MUL and 63:32 for the upper-half variants before\nregistering the multiply lane. Route the existing ALTOPS multiply\nformulas through the same lane on the same schedule. DIV and REM stay\nin the ordinary lane with the current launch and completion schedule.\nKeep the standalone ALU's default output behavior for the existing\narithmetic vectors and enable the split outputs in the core instance.\n\nAdd the formatted data-memory response as a parallel MEM-to-EX lane.\nUse address and width to select response bytes in parallel and apply\nsign extension directly from the selected byte or halfword sign bit.\nIn ID, compare both incoming source addresses against the destinations\nin EX and MEM. Latch the two pairs of matches with the instruction so\nthe comparisons are complete when the producers reach EX/MEM and\nMEM/WB. In EX, qualify those matches with the producer's actual writer\ncontrols and use mutually exclusive selects for the ordinary result,\nmultiply, load, older MEM/WB value and captured register-file value.\nGive the youngest eligible writer priority, exclude x0, and let an older\nwriter forward when a misaligned load traps. Merge the three result\ntypes at the MEM/WB register, so writeback and its EX bypass share one\nregistered value.\n\nRemove the decode load-use bubble. Hold EX/MEM and ID/EX, including the\ndependency matches, while an older memory request is unready. Retain\nthe MEM/WB data and writer qualification for forwarding under that hold\nand clear only retirement validity. On a ready edge, advance the load\nand its consumer together. A launched divide uses its captured operands\nthrough completion even as the older pipeline s\n…[8800 of 11872 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b771b6d1a726a05d]…\nGET=bench` passed all 132 cocotb cases, including 61 pipeline cases. Directed cases cover full-width LW chains, byte and halfword equality, signed ordering, raw unused operand values, and immediate corrections under memory and instruction stalls.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed selftest and all three random ELFs with and without bus stalls. CoreMark reported the canonical CRCs and its validation message.\n- `CORE_NAME=bench RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 ALTOPS checks with the single-channel wrapper.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` measured 81.130, 80.427, and 80.427 MHz across the three Gowin placements. CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,202,739 marker-bracketed cycles, yielding 251.12 iterations/s at the 80.427 MHz median.\n\nThe replay address path limits both placements at the median. The divider recurrence, ordered comparison, and register-backed shift paths are close to that limit. Compared with the starting core, the timed workload uses 10,630 more cycles.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
