{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261119-003-r12s2|hyp-20261119-001-r11s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(r[\\\"id\\\"], r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"], r[\\\"changes\\\"], sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\") for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-001-r11s0\nFor each byte of forwarded rs1 and the immediate, compute the sum with\ncarry-in zero. In the three upper bytes compute the carry-in-one sum\nin parallel, using the two operands with a preset carry-in. Derive the\nincoming byte carries with a short lookahead network using the\nuncarried sum's carry-out as generate and an all-ones operand XOR as\npropagate. Use each incoming carry to select the already computed\nbyte of the 32-bit redirect address. Clear bit zero for JALR.\n\nCompare both candidate sums of each upper byte to the fetch PC byte\nbefore selecting the match using the same incoming carry. Compare bits\n7:1 of the low byte and require fetch_pc[0] to be zero. Compute the\ncorresponding direct-target byte comparisons in parallel. Register\nfour selected byte predicates at the existing EX/MEM edge, with the\nparked-fetch qualifier, and reduce them in the recovery cycle. Use the\nassembled target for the existing alignment and BTB range checks.\n\nPreserve the EX/MEM hold, recovery, trap and retirement behavior. Prove\nboth the redirect sum and match against the original 32-bit expressions,\nincluding masked bit zero, wraparound and out-of-range target bits.\nAt 3,202,739 cycles promotion requires a median above 90.75 MHz. Measure\nall three Gowin placements and validate the bracketed CoreMark cycles and\nCRCs. The gain is a low-confidence projection given the near-tied paths.\n\n[{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Share precomputed carry-in-zero and carry-in-one byte sums and carry lookahead between the JALR redirect address and the four registered target-match predicates.'}]\nhyp-20261119-003-r12s2\nCheck the ordinary fetch candidate in parallel with architectural\nJALR target generation. Let A be the forwarded rs1, B the sign-extended\nimmediate and P the full candidate PC. For bits i from 1 through 31,\nthe required carry into bit i is C[i] = A[i] XOR B[i] XOR P[i]. Anchor\nC[1] to A[0] AND B[0] and require P[0] to be zero because JALR masks\nthe low sum bit. At each i from 1 through 30, independently check that\nC[i+1] equals (A[i] AND B[i]) OR ((A[i] OR B[i]) AND NOT P[i]).\nThe anchored carry recurrence proves equality modulo 32 bits.\n\nRegister four groups of carry-check predicates alongside the direct\ntarget predicates and the existing fall-through match. Select and reduce\nthe registered predicates in the recovery cycle with the parked-fetch\nqualifier. Generate the architectural JALR target from the ALU ADD\nlane, which already receives forwarded rs1 and the immediate for a\nlegal JALR. Use that full target for alignment, BTB eligibility, recovery\nand RVFI. Keep the resolution-valid pulse aligned to EX advance and\npreserve the existing same-cycle recovery and bus-stall semantics.\n\nA combinational SAT proof covered arbitrary 32-bit operands and candidate\nPCs, including odd immediates, wraparound and parked candidates. The\nshared-ADD scratch build passed stalled RVFI cosim on selftest and\nthree random programs. CoreMark validated all five CRCs with both bus\nstalls in 3,202,739 timed cycles. Gowin options 0, 1 and 2 measured\n79.348, 82.978 and 82.978 MHz, using 4,248 logic cells versus 4,393.\nThe critical path moved to the divider in both median placements. The\nmedian yields 259.08 iterations per second, down 4.35% from the champion.\nPromotion at these cycles requires median Fmax above 90.75 MHz.\nReproduce the timing sweep and run the single-retirement formal gates\non the eventual implementation.\n\n[{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Register grouped carry-consistency predicates to validate the full JALR fetch candidate in parallel with the architectural target from the existing ADD lane. Keep direct and fall-through checks, trap behavior, and the registered recovery schedule.'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
