n across EX/MEM\nhyp-20261119-002-r6s1 structural Retime result selection across EX/MEM\nhyp-20261119-003-r6s2 predictor Replay two instruction words at predicted taken targets\nhyp-20261119-001-r7s0 micro_opt Compute AUIPC in ID to remove the EX operand mux\nhyp-20261119-002-r7s1 structural Route immediate load forwarding through branch and address lanes\nhyp-20261119-003-r7s2 predictor Read BTB target replay one fetch ahead\nhyp-20261119-001-r8s0 micro_opt Select the forwarded load byte with a registered index\nhyp-20261119-002-r8s1 structural Register load forwarding outside equality branches\nhyp-20261119-003-r8\n…[23097 of 26169 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a59db9402f9294d5]…\n buses.\n- Stalled CoreMark validated all five CRCs without an out-of-bounds access. The start and stop markers were at cycles 12,468 and 3,215,207, giving 3,202,739 timed cycles.\n- The single-retirement `formal/run_all.sh` gate passed all 53 checks on the final RTL, including the depth-20 register-consistency check. It used `wrapper_si.sv` and `checks_si.cfg` in a scratch copy. No formal fixes were needed.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| RTL | Option 0 | Option 1 | Option 2 | Median Fmax | Logic cells |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Champion rerun | 76.343 MHz | 86.757 MHz | 86.757 MHz | 86.757 MHz | 4,393 |\n| Parallel carry checks | 76.896 MHz | 79.924 MHz | 79.924 MHz | 79.924 MHz | 4,342 |\n\nThe divider's partial-remainder feedback limits options 1 and 2. The fetch replay path limits option 0. At the measured cycle count the median gives 249.55 CoreMark iterations/s, 7.88% below the champion. The median also falls short of the supplied scratch result of 82.978 MHz and the 90.75 MHz promotion threshold.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
