{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv && cat cores/bench/core.yaml && ls -la /srv/hwebench/tmp/7cb5c576/e0d5a92c'","aggregated_output":"// rtl/reg_file.sv\n//\n// 32 x 32 RV32I integer register file.\n//   - x0 hardwired to zero (writes silently dropped, reads always 0).\n//   - Two combinational read ports.\n//   - Single synchronous write port.\n//   - Write-first bypass: a same-cycle write to the read address returns\n//     the new value. This matches the prior Chisel core's RegFile.scala\n//     and lets the ID stage see WB-stage writes within the same cycle\n//     without an extra forwarding mux.\n//\n// The reset clears all 32 registers. Distributed-LUT or flop inference is\n// fine here; explicit BRAM attribution lives on the larger imem/dmem\n// declarations in soc.sv (phase 5).\n//\n// Latency:        write = 1 cycle (synchronous), read = combinational.\n// RVFI fields:    feeds rs1_rdata, rs2_rdata, rd_wdata.\nmodule reg_file (\n  input  logic        clock,\n  input  logic        reset,\n\n  input  logic [4:0]  rs1_addr,\n  input  logic [4:0]  rs2_addr,\n  output logic [31:0] rs1_data,\n  output logic [31:0] rs2_data,\n\n  input  logic        w_en,\n  input  logic [4:0]  w_addr,\n  input  logic [31:0] w_data\n);\n\n  logic [31:0] regs [0:31];\n  logic write_reg;\n  logic bypass_rs1, bypass_rs2, read_rs1, read_rs2;\n\n  assign write_reg = w_en && w_addr != 5'b0;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) begin\n      for (int i = 0; i < 32; i++) regs[i] <= 32'b0;\n    end else if (write_reg) begin\n      regs[w_addr] <= w_data;\n    end\n  end\n\n  // Resolve x0 and write-first priority in the one-hot read enables.\n  assign bypass_rs1 = write_reg && w_addr == rs1_addr;\n  assign bypass_rs2 = write_reg && w_addr == rs2_addr;\n  assign read_rs1 = rs1_addr != 5'b0 && !bypass_rs1;\n  assign read_rs2 = rs2_addr != 5'b0 && !bypass_rs2;\n\n  assign rs1_data = ({32{read_rs1}} & regs[rs1_addr]) | ({32{bypass_rs1}} & w_data);\n  assign rs2_data = ({32{read_rs2}} & regs[rs2_addr]) | ({32{bypass_rs2}} & w_data);\n\nendmodule\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 86.757\n  lut4: 4393\n  ff: 994\n  coremark_iter_s: 3.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261119-003-r10s2\n  updated: '2026-11-19T20:51:04.798791Z'\ntotal 24\ndrwxrwx---+  7 nobody    nogroup   4096 Nov 20 01:24 .\ndrwxrwx---+  5 nobody    nogroup   4096 Nov 20 01:23 ..\ndr-xr-xr-x   2 hwebench2 hwebench2   40 Nov 20 01:24 .agents\ndr-xr-xr-x   2 hwebench2 hwebench2   40 Nov 20 01:24 .aws\ndr-xr-xr-x   2 hwebench2 hwebench2   40 Nov 20 01:24 .codex\ndr-xr-xr-x   2 hwebench2 hwebench2   40 Nov 20 01:24 .git\ndrwxrwx---+ 12 hwebench2 hwebench2 4096 Nov 20 01:24 codex-bwrap-synthetic-mount-targets-1002\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
