e corresponding quotient bit. Select the quotient or remainder after the last update, apply the appropriate sign for signed operations, and transfer it through the usual EX/MEM boundary. Handle zero divisors and INT_MIN divided by -1 with their exact RV32M results on the same schedule. Keep multiply and RV32I on the single-cycle ALU path so matrix multiplication, address generation and ordinary dependencies incur no new EX latency.\\n\\nLaunch once from a valid divide/remainder in ID/EX when the ol\n…[31605 of 34677 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:12482a0e192f7b3f]…\n retain the current replay word and hit in a local\\nregister. This removes replay-hit and squash feedback from the replay\\nread addresses.\\n\\nExtract rs1 and rs2 addresses directly from the ready bus word, the\\nretained word, and each replay result. Read the register file from\\nthese candidates in parallel. Select the instruction and its two\\noperand values together with the same one-hot source selection at\\nID/EX. A ready bus response has priority. The normal decoder and\\ndestination-match logic consume the selected instruction. Give each\\noperand lane the existing write-first and x0 behavior. Read fresh\\noperand values even when the selected instruction word was held.\\nThis keeps word selection out of the register-file address path\\nwithout adding a cycle between fetch and issue.\\n\\nRegister the ordinary candidate PC and its parked bit with the resolved\\nJALR target at EX/MEM. Compare the registered full-width addresses in\\nthe recovery cycle and use the result to select the corresponding\\nrepla regression\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
