{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'riscv|gowin|coremark' Makefile | head -70 && cat formal/checks_si.cfg && cat fpga/core_bench_si.sv\"", "aggregated_output": "42:  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\n80:\t@echo \"  make formal TARGET=v1   — riscv-formal fast suite (with ALTOPS)\"\n84:\t@echo \"  make bench              — build selftest + coremark ELFs\"\n112:cosim: cosim-build bench/programs/selftest.elf bench/programs/coremark.elf\n136:# (tools/eval/gowin.py); V2 does not synthesize with Yosys.\n137:fpga: cosim-build bench/programs/coremark.elf\n141:\tpython3 -m tools.eval.gowin $(TARGET)\n143:bench/programs/coremark.elf: bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/crt0.S \\\n144:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.c) \\\n145:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.h) \\\n146:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.c) \\\n147:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.h)\n148:\t$(MAKE) -f bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/coremark.elf\n162:\t  [ -e \"$(WT_PATH)/formal/riscv-formal\" ] || ln -s \"$(CURDIR)/formal/riscv-formal\" \"$(WT_PATH)/formal/riscv-formal\"; \\\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill    