an\naccepted, live slot and preserve same-index update bypasses.\n\nCompute three IF successors in parallel from the normal request,\nregistered target and registered fall-through using separate read\nports on the same logical BTB. Qualify the pending update and check\nthe tag for each candidate before the late recovery mux. Select the\npresented address, PC+4 and predictor metadata from the same\ncandidate. This gives the late branch decision one output mux to\nsteer and keeps a corrected \n…[9248 of 12320 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4aa7bd6f2f43278b]…\n and suppress it if the younger\nrequest is parked or invalidated. Use the existing full-width adder,\nalignment handling, and resolved target for recovery, training and\nRVFI. An absent or failed operand check takes the existing JALR\nrecovery path, including the rare case where an unpredicted target\ncoincides with PC+4. Direct branches and JAL continue comparing their\nactual full-width successors. Keep a single EX-advance pulse for\nrecovery and training, and preserve reset, FENCE.I and bus stall\npriority.\n\nThis places the inverse arithmetic before ID/EX, leaving only an\noperand comparison on the forwarded validation path. An EX-local\ninverse arithmetic trial reached 76.827 MHz in Gowin option 1, with\nthe divider recurrence limiting timing. The divider and replay\npaths remain risks. At near unchanged cycles a median above 90.75 MHz\nclears promotion. The 5% estimate assumes about 91.2 MHz with little\nadded recovery cost. Measure the new ID setup path and the actual\nrate of absent checks before judging the gain.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
