{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_58", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r13s0','r10s1','r9s2')):\n  print(r['id'])\n  print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261119-003-r9s2\nExpand the predictor-armed instruction replay store to 4,096 words and\npack each entry's valid bit, full PC[19:14] tag and 32-bit instruction\ninto one 39-bit RAM word. Index by PC[13:2]. Keep the synchronous read\naligned to the next ordinary fetch PC so validity arrives with the\nword. Use a sequential scrub on reset and each advancing FENCE.I to\nwrite invalid entries through the existing RAM write port. Drive the\ntag and payload directly from the bus-side fill signals on every\nwrite, since the scrub only needs to write validity to zero. Gate all\nreplay hits while the scrub is active, starting in the invalidation\ncycle. Restart the scrub at zero on each invalidation and enable hits\nonly after the last write completes. Fetch and retire through the\nnormal imem path while scrubbing. Record taken prediction or taken\nrecovery arming during the scrub and resume fills once it completes.\n\nGive scrub writes priority over fills. Otherwise preserve refresh\nfrom accepted ready imem responses with a fill enable independent of\nreplay hit. Carry the sampled write index and strobe alongside the\nread to reject read/write collisions across all twelve index bits.\nKeep exact aligned in-range PC qualification, bus-first acceptance,\nrecovery and parking behavior, and full-width EX validation. FENCE.I\nstill forces a fall-through refetch and clears the arm with priority.\n\nScratch Gowin placements reached 68.623, 74.642 and 74.642 MHz,\nusing 3,482 logic cells, 926 registers and 14 BSRAMs in option 0.\nThis is 1,767 fewer logic cells and seven more BSRAMs than the\nchampion. The reported median-placement bottleneck remained data RAM\nto the EX shifter. Scratch CoreMark took 3,183,041 marker-bracketed\ncycles with the canonical CRCs, giving 234.50 iter/s, up 0.79%.\nPromotion at these cycles requires a median above 77.47 MHz, so the\nmeasured result leaves a timing gap of 2.83 MHz. The prototype matched\nthe reference RVFI traces on selftest and all three random programs\nwith and without stalls. Two directed cases passed for \n…[4261 of 7333 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:23dbd521a1c52e6e]…\nthe last word, BTB training and single-channel retirement.\n\nA preliminary word-and-tag snapshot prototype passed short RVFI\ncosim and validated stalled CoreMark at the champion's cycle count.\nGowin placements measured 74.415, 82.692 and 82.692 MHz, with the\nreplay-output-to-register-file path limiting the median. It also\nfailed a directed FENCE.I fetch-sequence assertion. The proposal\nsaves the fully qualified hit instead of reconstructing validity from\nheld metadata. A scratch implementation passed all 61 unchanged\npipeline tests, including that FENCE.I regression, and eight short\nRVFI cosim cases. Stalled CoreMark validated all CRCs in 3,202,739\nbracketed cycles.\nPromotion at the champion's cycle count requires a median above\n90.75 MHz. A median of 91.1 MHz would yield about 284.4 iter/s.\nThe near-tied divider and EX paths make that an unverified target.\nRun the existing collision, FENCE.I, parking and stall tests, check\nthe full RVFI gates and canonical CoreMark CRCs, and time all three\nGowin placements.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_59", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'trial_select=$(mktemp -d \"$TMPDIR/bench-r15s1-select.XXXXXX\") &&\nmkdir -p \"$trial_select/cores/bench\" &&\ncp -r cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/core.yaml \"$trial_select/cores/bench/\" &&\ncp -r fpga \"$trial_select/\" &&\npython3 - \"$trial_select\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr = Path(sys.argv[1]) / 'cores/bench/rtl'\ndef edit(name, pairs):\n    p = r / name\n    s = p.read_text()\n    for a, b in pairs:\n        assert s.count(a) == 1, (name, a)\n        s = s.replace(a, b)\n    p.write_text(s)\n\nedit('core_pkg.sv', [\n    ('    logic [1:0]  ex_match;      // {rs2, rs1}, producer advances to EX/MEM\\\\n    logic [1:0]  mem_match;     // {rs2, rs1}, producer advances to MEM/WB', '    fwd_sel_t    rs1_select;\\\\n    fwd_sel_t    rs2_select;'),\n])\nedit('ex_stage.sv', [\n    ('  output ex_mem_t             out,', '  output ex_mem_t             out,\\\\n  output logic               next_write,\\\\n  output result_sel_t        next_selection,'),\n    ('  assign out = reg_q;', '  assign out = reg_q;\\\\n  assign next_write = in.valid && mem_ctrl.reg_write && \"'!mem_misalign;'\"\\\\n  assign next_selection = result_sel;'),\n])\nedit('id_stage.sv', [\n    ('  input  logic [4:0]        mem_rd,', '  input  logic [4:0]        mem_rd,\\\\n  input  logic              ex_write,\\\\n  input  logic              mem_write,\\\\n  input  result_sel_t       ex_selection,'),\n    ('  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\\\\n    if (reset)', '''  logic [1:0] youngest, older;\n  fwd_sel_t selected_rs1, selected_rs2, replay_sel_rs1, replay_sel_rs2;\n\n  assign youngest = {2{ex_write && \"'!squash_candidate}}\n                  & {rs2_addr != 5'\"'b0 && rs2_addr == ex_rd,\n                     rs1_addr \"'!= 5'\"'b0 && rs1_addr == ex_rd};\n  assign older = {2{mem_write}} & ~youngest\n               & {rs2_addr \"'!= 5'\"'b0 && rs2_addr == mem_rd,\n                  rs1_addr \"'!= 5'\"'b0 && rs1_addr == mem_rd};\n\n  assign selected_rs1.result = youngest[0] ? ex_selection : '0;\n  assign selected_rs2.result = youngest[1] ? ex_selection : '0;\n  assign {selected_rs1.wb, selected_rs2.wb} = {older[0], older[1]};\n  assign {selected_rs1.regfile, selected_rs2.regfile} = {\n      \"'!youngest[0] && !older[0], !youngest[1] && !older[1]};\n  assign replay_sel_rs1 = {6'\"'b0, replay_load_match[0], \"'!replay_load_match[0]};\n  assign replay_sel_rs2 = {6'\"'b0, replay_load_match[1], \"'!replay_load_match[1]};\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset)'\"'''),\n    ('''      reg_q.ex_match      <= {rs2_addr \"'!= 5'\"'b0 && rs2_addr == ex_rd,\n                              rs1_addr \"'!= 5'\"'b0 && rs1_addr == ex_rd};\n      reg_q.mem_match     <= {rs2_addr \"'!= 5'\"'b0 && rs2_addr == mem_rd,\n                              rs1_addr \"'!= 5'\"'b0 && rs1_addr == mem_rd};''',\n     '''      reg_q.rs1_select    <= selected_rs1;\n      reg_q.rs2_select    <= selected_rs2;'''),\n    ('''        reg_q.ex_match  <= '0;\n        reg_q.mem_match <= replay_load_match;''',\n     '''        reg_q.rs1_select <= replay_sel_rs1;\n        reg_q.rs2_select <= replay_sel_rs2;'''),\n])\nedit('core.sv', [\n    ('  logic        mem_request, mem_write_en;', '  logic        mem_request, mem_write_en, ex_write_en;\\\\n  result_sel_t ex_selection;'),\n    ('    .mem_rd           (ex_mem_w.rd),', '    .mem_rd           (ex_mem_w.rd),\\\\n    .ex_write         (ex_write_en),\\\\n    .mem_write        (mem_write_en),\\\\n    .ex_selection    (ex_selection),'),\n    ('    .out              (ex_mem_w),', '    .out              (ex_mem_w),\\\\n    .next_write       (ex_write_en),\\\\n    .next_selection   (ex_selection),'),\n    ('''  forward_unit u_fwd (\n    .ex_match    (id_ex_w.ex_match),\n    .mem_match   (id_ex_w.mem_match),\n    .ex_mem_w_en (mem_write_en),\n    .ex_mem_sel  (ex_mem_w.result_sel),\n    .mem_wb_w_en (mem_wb_w.reg_write),\n    .fwd_rs1     (fwd_rs1_sel),\n    .fwd_rs2     (fwd_rs2_sel)\n  );''', '''  assign fwd_rs1_sel = id_ex_w.rs1_select;\n  assign fwd_rs2_sel = id_ex_w.rs2_select;'''),\n])\nprint(sys.argv[1])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
